/frame :ws/value       | Same in principle; representing the envelope and D in columnar form   |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.codec.md:534:| Batching                | None needed; one value per frame.                           | A record batch **is** one value. Batching many stream values into     |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.codec.md:535:|                         |                                                             | one frame would change append semantics (one `append!`, one frame)    |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.codec.md:542:dictionaries, or self-contained per-frame IPC payloads. The two mechanisms\ndocs/design/dao.stream.codec.md:554:## 6. The callsites and the stability promise\ndocs/design/dao.stream.codec.md:556:### 6.1 What \"swap without breaking client callsites\" promises, precisely\ndocs/design/dao.stream.codec.md:584:### 6.2 Callsite table\ndocs/design/dao.stream.codec.md:616:### 6.3 Lanes\ndocs/design/dao.stream.codec.md:639:### 6.4 Which codec yin.repl selects by default: owner decision\ndocs/design/dao.stream.codec.md:654:frames are readable in a browser devtools pane; Transit admits identifiers\ndocs/design/dao.stream.codec.md:660:## 7. Migration\ndocs/design/dao.stream.codec.md:662:### 7.1 Slices: expand, migrate, contract\ndocs/design/dao.stream.codec.md:695:|       |          | `dao.stream.ws` (gate, `codec-index`, `distinct?` check, frame kind,        | cases for nil, `{}` and a **malformed** profile (a key missing,     |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.codec.md:703:|       |          |                                                                             | ':ws/\\(subprotocol\\|frame-kind\\|portable-value?\\|encode\\|decode\\)'` |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.codec.md:728:|       |          | `:ws/*` keys plus one added `:ws/bytes?` boolean (the capability of §3.3    | is **conditional on OQ3**: under the move, `grep ':ws/\\(frame-kind  |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.codec.md:754:### 7.2 Test impact (V, grep of `test/` on 2026-10-20)\ndocs/design/dao.stream.