{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc | sed -n '421,820p'\"","aggregated_output":"   421\t(defn without-runner\n   422\t  \"The store handle the shell keeps: `open`'s answer without the node,\n   423\t   which the shell carries as its own `:dht`.  Any other handle is\n   424\t   answered as it is.\"\n   425\t  [handle]\n   426\t  (dissoc handle :dht))\n   427\t\n   428\t\n   429\t(defn follower\n   430\t  \"The head follower the shell's DHT `node` carries, or nil when it\n   431\t   follows nothing.\"\n   432\t  [node]\n   433\t  (get node ::follower))\n   434\t\n   435\t\n   436\t(defn stop!\n   437\t  \"Initiate the head composition's exit on the shell's node: the board's\n   438\t   server is asked to stop (`head.board/stop!`), every follow dial is\n   439\t   closed and no dial is composed again, and the node is marked\n   440\t   stopping.  Performs no other I/O; `step` completes the stop and\n   441\t   `stopped?` reports it.  A shell without a node, or already stopping,\n   442\t   is answered unchanged.  The board serves a read-only ring that stop\n   443\t   does not end, so a reader has nothing to be told but the reattachable\n   444\t   close its connection observes.\"\n   445\t  [shell]\n   446\t  (let [node (:dht shell)]\n   447\t    (if (or (nil? node) (::stopping? node))\n   448\t      shell\n   449\t      (do (doseq [[_ {:keys [dial]}] (get-in node [::follow :links])]\n   450\t            (when dial (head.board/close! dial)))\n   451\t          (assoc shell :dht\n   452\t                 (cond-> (assoc node ::stopping? true)\n   453\t                   (get-in node [::publisher :server])\n   454\t                   (update-in [::publisher :server] head.board/stop!)\n   455\t\n   456\t                   (::follow node)\n   457\t                   (assoc-in [::follow :links] {})))))))\n   458\t\n   459\t\n   460\t(defn stopped?\n   461\t  \"True when the head composition owes nothing at exit: no node, no\n   462\t   board server, or a board server that is stopped or refused.\"\n   463\t  [shell]\n   464\t  (let [server (get-in shell [:dht ::publisher :server])]\n   465\t    (or (nil? server) (head.board/stopped? server))))\n   466\t\n   467\t\n   468\t(defn close!\n   469\t  \"The last resort after the exit drain's budget\n   470\t   (`yin.repl.main/stop-ticks`): whatever the board still owes is asked\n   471\t   for once more and not awaited.  The ordinary exit is `stop!`, then\n   472\t   `step` until `stopped?`.  A shell never stopped is stopped first, so a\n   473\t   direct caller (a test, an embedder without a drain) still closes the\n   474\t   dials; the board's stopping tick runs at the node's last tick reading\n   475\t   only when the board is not already `stopped?`.\"\n   476\t  [shell]\n   477\t  (let [shell (stop! shell)\n   478\t        node (:dht shell)\n   479\t        server (get-in node [::publisher :server])]\n   480\t    (when (and server (not (head.board/stopped? server)))\n   481\t      (head.board/serve-step server (or (::now node) 0)))\n   482\t    nil))\n   483\t\n   484\t\n   485\t;; =============================================================================\n   486\t;; Lines\n   487\t;; =============================================================================\n   488\t\n   489\t(defn- address-text\n   490\t  [host port]\n   491\t  (if (str/includes? host \":\") (str \"[\" host \"]:\" port) (str host \":\" port)))\n   492\t\n   493\t\n   494\t(defn- reason-text\n   495\t  \"One blob's failure reason as the REPL prints it.\"\n   496\t  [node {:keys [reason peers]}]\n   497\t  (case reason\n   498\t    :dao.jing.dht/solo (str \"solo: no --dht-peer is configured, so nothing \"\n   499\t                            \"was sent; the index is in \" (::dir node) \" only\")\n   500\t    :dao.jing.dht/unpublished (str \"publication is off: this node fetches \"\n   501\t                                   \"only; start with --dht-publish to share\")\n   502\t    :dao.jing.dht/too-few-peers (str \"too few peers, sent to \" peers \" of \"\n   503\t                                     (dht/ack-peers node) \" before the \"\n   504\t                                     \"acknowledgement deadline\")\n   505\t    :dao.jing.dht/oversize \"a blob exceeds the DHT message bound\"\n   506\t    :dao.jing.dht/absent \"a blob was no longer in the local store\"\n   507\t    :dao.jing.dht/busy \"too many writes were pending\"\n   508\t    :dao.space.dht/backlog-full \"the replicate backlog was full\"\n   509\t    :dao.space.dht/publications-full (str \"too many publications awaited \"\n   510\t                                          \"their first report\")\n   511\t    :dao.space.dht/cancelled \"cancelled\"\n   512\t    (str reason)))\n   513\t\n   514\t\n   515\t(def ^:private ended-text\n   516\t  {:dao.space.dht/terminal \"every remaining failure is final\"\n   517\t   :dao.space.dht/cancelled \"cancelled\"\n   518\t   :dao.space.dht/displaced \"displaced by newer publications\"})\n   519\t\n   520\t\n   521\t(defn- result-text\n   522\t  \"A publication's result (yin.vm.linker.dht.md 5.5.6): when it is not\n   523\t   acknowledged, the count of failed blobs, the first reason, and whether\n   524\t   the node is retrying.\"\n   525\t  [node {:keys [result blobs peers failed repairing? ended]}]\n   526\t  (if (= :acknowledged result)\n   527\t    (str \"acknowledged: sent to \" peers \" peers\")\n   528\t    (str (if (= :partial result)\n   529\t           \"PARTIAL: the manifest was sent; \"\n   530\t           \"NOT acknowledged: \")\n   531\t         (reason-text node (first failed))\n   532\t         \"; \" (count failed) \" of \" blobs \" blobs not sent\"\n   533\t         (cond\n   534\t           repairing? \"; retrying while the node is open\"\n   535\t           ended (str \"; not retrying (\" (get ended-text ended (str ended)) \")\")\n   536\t           :else \"; not retrying\")\n   537\t         \"; the local copy is durable\")))\n   538\t\n   539\t\n   540\t(defn- failure-text\n   541\t  \"A load's failure reason, data (dao.space.dht 4.3), as text.\"\n   542\t  [{:dao.space.dht/keys [failure] :keys [address cause defect outcome]\n   543\t    :as reason}]\n   544\t  (case failure\n   545\t    :miss (str \"no peer produced \" address \" (\" (name cause) \")\")\n   546\t    :invalid (str \"the content \" (when address (str \"at \" address \" \"))\n   547\t                  \"is invalid (\" (:code defect) \")\"\n   548\t                  (when-let [text (:text defect)] (str \": \" text)))\n   549\t    :unaskable (str \"could not ask for \" address \" (\" (name outcome) \")\")\n   550\t    (pr-str (if (nil? failure) reason failure))))\n   551\t\n   552\t\n   553\t(defn- event-line\n   554\t  [node {:keys [manifest blobs host port id reason datoms fetched], :as event}]\n   555\t  (case (::dht/event event)\n   556\t    :bound (str \"dht: node \" (subs id 0 16) \" listening on \"\n   557\t                (address-text host port) \"; peers: \"\n   558\t                (str/join \", \" (map #(address-text (:host %) (:port %))\n   559\t                                    (:peers node)))\n   560\t                (if (:publish? node) \"; publishing\" \"; fetch-only\"))\n   561\t    :bind-failed (str \"dht: refused: the socket could not bind: \" reason)\n   562\t    (:published :republished)\n   563\t    (str \"dht: \" (name (::dht/event event)) \" \" manifest \" (\" blobs \" blobs), \"\n   564\t         (result-text node event))\n   565\t    :publication-unknown (str \"dht: published \" manifest\n   566\t                              \", acknowledgement unknown: facts were lost\")\n   567\t    :loaded (str (if (= manifest (::hydrating node)) \"dht: hydrated \"\n   568\t                     \"dht: loaded \")\n   569\t                 manifest \", \"\n   570\t                 (when datoms (str datoms \" datoms, \"))\n   571\t                 fetched \" blobs fetched\"\n   572\t                 (when (= manifest (::hydrating node)) \"; evaluation admitted\"))\n   573\t    :load-failed (str \"dht: \" (if (= manifest (::hydrating node)) \"refused: \"\n   574\t                                  \"\")\n   575\t                      \"loading \" manifest \" failed: \" (failure-text reason)\n   576\t                      (when (= manifest (::hydrating node))\n   577\t                        \"; the remote index was not hydrated\"))\n   578\t    (pr-str event)))\n   579\t\n   580\t\n   581\t(defn join-token\n   582\t  \"The one string a reader hands `yin-repl dht join`: the publishing\n   583\t   node's address and its principal's 64 hex digits, as\n   584\t   `yin:<host:port>/<principal>` (5.8).  It names no manifest: a reader\n   585\t   follows the head the principal publishes.\"\n   586\t  [host port principal]\n   587\t  (str \"yin:\" (address-text host port) \"/\" principal))\n   588\t\n   589\t\n   590\t(defn- trace-text\n   591\t  [trace]\n   592\t  (let [{:yin.head/keys [manifest] n :yin.head/seq} (:yin.head/envelope trace)]\n   593\t    (str manifest \" (seq \" n \")\")))\n   594\t\n   595\t\n   596\t(defn- head-line\n   597\t  \"A follower event (`yin.vm.linker.head`) as the line the REPL prints,\n   598\t   or nil.\"\n   599\t  [{:keys [principal trace reason failure outcome detail delay] :as e}]\n   600\t  (case (:yin.head/event e)\n   601\t    :installed (str \"dht: installed the head of \" principal \": \"\n   602\t                    (trace-text trace))\n   603\t    :refused (str \"dht: refused a head of \" principal \": \" reason\n   604\t                  (when (map? trace) (str \", \" (trace-text trace))))\n   605\t    :unloadable (str \"dht: the head of \" principal \" \" (trace-text trace)\n   606\t                     \" cannot load: \" (failure-text failure)\n   607\t                     \"; trying again after the repair delay\")\n   608\t    :source-lost (str \"dht: lost the head board of \" principal \" (\"\n   609\t                      (pr-str outcome) \"); dialing it again\")\n   610\t    :unpersisted (str \"dht: the head of \" principal \" \" (trace-text trace)\n   611\t                      \" is not installed: :yin.head/unpersisted (\" detail\n   612\t                      \"); writing \" heads-file \" again in \" delay \" ticks\")\n   613\t    nil))\n   614\t\n   615\t\n   616\t;; =============================================================================\n   617\t;; The board endpoint and the token (5.1, 5.8)\n   618\t;; =============================================================================\n   619\t\n   620\t(def ^:private board-codec\n   621\t  \"The head board's wire profile.\"\n   622\t  (:transit connect/codec-profiles))\n   623\t\n   624\t\n   625\t(defn- serve-board\n   626\t  \"Compose the board's endpoint once the node's socket is bound at\n   627\t   `host`:`port`: `[pub lines]`.\"\n   628\t  [pub ws host port]\n   629\t  (let [server (head.board/serve {:board (:board pub)\n   630\t                                  :principal (:principal pub)\n   631\t                                  :spec {:host host :port port}\n   632\t                                  :host ws\n   633\t                                  :codecs [board-codec]})]\n   634\t    [(assoc pub :server server :listen [host port])\n   635\t     (when (= :refused (:status server))\n   636\t       [(case (:reason server)\n   637\t          :yin.head/not-loopback\n   638\t          (str \"dht: the head board is served on loopback only; this node \"\n   639\t               \"binds \" host \", so it serves no board and prints no token\")\n   640\t          :dao.stream.remote-channel/no-transport\n   641\t          \"dht: this host has no WebSocket listener: no head board, no token\"\n   642\t          (str \"dht: the head board could not bind TCP \"\n   643\t               (address-text host port) \": no board, no join token; \"\n   644\t               \"choose another --dht-port\"))])]))\n   645\t\n   646\t\n   647\t(defn- stopped-line\n   648\t  \"The board's end, printed once on its transition to stopped.\"\n   649\t  [outcome]\n   650\t  (if (= :confirmed outcome)\n   651\t    \"dht: the head board stopped\"\n   652\t    (str \"dht: the head board stopped without host completion (\"\n   653\t         (name outcome) \")\")))\n   654\t\n   655\t\n   656\t(defn- step-board\n   657\t  \"Advance the board's endpoint, print the token once when it is bound,\n   658\t   the board's end once when it stops, and each deposit refusal:\n   659\t   `[pub lines]`.  A stopping node composes no board.\"\n   660\t  [pub node events now]\n   661\t  (let [bound (some #(when (= :bound (::dht/event %)) %) events)\n   662\t        [pub lines] (if (and bound (nil? (:server pub)) (not (::stopping? node)))\n   663\t                      (serve-board pub (::ws node) (:host bound) (:port bound))\n   664\t                      [pub nil])\n   665\t        before (get-in pub [:server :status])\n   666\t        server (when (:server pub) (head.board/serve-step (:server pub) now))\n   667\t        pub (cond-> pub server (assoc :server server))\n   668\t        [host port] (:listen pub)\n   669\t        lines (cond-> (vec lines)\n   670\t                (and (= :serving (:status server)) (not (:token? pub)))\n   671\t                (conj (str \"dht: join token: \"\n   672\t                           (join-token host port (:public (:key pub)))))\n   673\t\n   674\t                (and (= :refused (:status server)) (not= :refused before))\n   675\t                (conj (str \"dht: the head board could not bind TCP \"\n   676\t                           (address-text host port) \": no board, no join \"\n   677\t                           \"token; choose another --dht-port\"))\n   678\t\n   679\t                (and (= :stopped (:status server)) (not= :stopped before))\n   680\t                (conj (stopped-line (get-in server [:stop :outcome]))))\n   681\t        pub (cond-> pub (= :serving (:status server)) (assoc :token? true))\n   682\t        ;; a gap means refusals were evicted unread: adopt its recovery\n   683\t        ;; cursor, say so, and drain what the ring still holds\n   684\t        [notes lost? cursor] (loop [notes [] lost? false\n   685\t                                    cursor (:notes-cursor pub)]\n   686\t                               (let [r (stream/next (:notes pub) cursor)]\n   687\t                                 (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\n   688\t                                   :dao.stream/ok (recur (conj notes\n   689\t                                                               (:dao.stream/value r))\n   690\t                                                         lost?\n   691\t                                                         (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n   692\t                                   :dao.stream/gap (recur notes true\n   693\t                                                          (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n   694\t                                   [notes lost? cursor])))]\n   695\t    [(assoc pub :notes-cursor cursor)\n   696\t     (-> lines\n   697\t         (cond-> lost? (conj (str \"dht: more head trace refusals arrived \"\n   698\t                                  \"than could be kept; the oldest were not \"\n   699\t                                  \"reported\")))\n   700\t         (into (map (fn [{:keys [reason manifest]}]\n   701\t                      (str \"dht: the head trace of \" manifest \" was not \"\n   702\t                           \"deposited: \" reason)))\n   703\t               notes))]))\n   704\t\n   705\t\n   706\t(defn- hydrated\n   707\t  \"Install the loaded remote index as this directory's: HEAD first, then\n   708\t   the indexer, exactly as a restart's recovery is installed.  A\n   709\t   publisher deposits the hydrated HEAD's trace once (5.4).\"\n   710\t  [shell node]\n   711\t  (let [manifest (::hydrating node)\n   712\t        recovery {:manifest manifest :datoms (dht/loaded-datoms node manifest)}]\n   713\t    ((:head-fn (dht/local node)) manifest)\n   714\t    (when-some [pub (::publisher node)]\n   715\t      (deposit-head! pub manifest))\n   716\t    (-> shell\n   717\t        (update :indexer index/rehydrate recovery)\n   718\t        (assoc :index-recovery recovery\n   719\t               :dht (dissoc node ::hydrating)))))\n   720\t\n   721\t\n   722\t;; =============================================================================\n   723\t;; Following (5.3, 5.5, 5.7)\n   724\t;; =============================================================================\n   725\t\n   726\t(defn- next-delay\n   727\t  [follower delay]\n   728\t  (if delay\n   729\t    (min (* 2 delay) (:repair-max-ticks follower))\n   730\t    (:repair-ticks follower)))\n   731\t\n   732\t\n   733\t(defn- drop-dial\n   734\t  \"Close the dial of a link and schedule the next one after its delay;\n   735\t   the last failure reported is kept.\"\n   736\t  [follower link now]\n   737\t  (when-some [d (:dial link)] (head.board/close! d))\n   738\t  (let [delay (next-delay follower (:delay link))]\n   739\t    {:due (+ now delay) :delay delay :failed (:failed link)}))\n   740\t\n   741\t\n   742\t(defn- lost-reason\n   743\t  \"What ended a lost dial, as one keyword: the remote's reason, or the\n   744\t   outcome.\"\n   745\t  [d]\n   746\t  (let [o (:outcome d)]\n   747\t    (or (:dao.stream.remote/reason o) (:dao.stream/outcome o) :lost)))\n   748\t\n   749\t\n   750\t(defn- dial-line\n   751\t  \"The line a dial failure prints when it differs from the last one.\"\n   752\t  [principal {:keys [host port]} failure]\n   753\t  (str \"dht: cannot follow \" principal \" at \" (address-text host port) \": \"\n   754\t       (case failure\n   755\t         :dao.stream.remote/not-found\n   756\t         \"that endpoint serves no head board for this principal\"\n   757\t         :dao.stream.remote/channel-gone\n   758\t         \"the connection was refused, closed, or stopped answering\"\n   759\t         :dao.stream.remote-channel/no-transport\n   760\t         \"this host has no WebSocket dialer\"\n   761\t         (str failure))\n   762\t       \"; dialing it again\"))\n   763\t\n   764\t\n   765\t(defn- step-link\n   766\t  \"Advance the dial of `principal`'s board at `now`: compose one when\n   767\t   due, step it, hand a fresh reflection to the follower, and redial a\n   768\t   dial that is lost.  Liveness is the channel's: a resolve or a read\n   769\t   left unanswered for the link's `give-up-after` is lost as\n   770\t   channel-gone.  Only the address the principal was given is dialed.\n   771\t   Answers `[follower link failure]`, `failure` the keyword that ended a\n   772\t   dial this step, or nil.\"\n   773\t  [follower ws source link now]\n   774\t  (cond\n   775\t    (and (nil? (:dial link)) (some? (:due link)) (< now (:due link)))\n   776\t    [follower link nil]\n   777\t\n   778\t    (nil? (:dial link))\n   779\t    (let [d (head.board/dial {:principal (sign/principal (:principal source))\n   780\t                              :spec {:host (:host source)\n   781\t                                     :port (:port source)}\n   782\t                              :host ws\n   783\t                              :codec board-codec})]\n   784\t      (if (= :refused (:status d))\n   785\t        [follower (drop-dial follower link now) (:reason d)]\n   786\t        [follower (assoc link :dial d :handle nil) nil]))\n   787\t\n   788\t    :else\n   789\t    (let [d (head.board/dial-step (:dial link) now)\n   790\t          link (assoc link :dial d)\n   791\t          h (head.board/handle d)]\n   792\t      (cond\n   793\t        (and h (not (identical? h (:handle link))))\n   794\t        [(head/attach follower (sign/principal (:principal source)) h)\n   795\t         (assoc link :handle h :delay nil :failed nil)\n   796\t         nil]\n   797\t\n   798\t        (= :lost (:status d))\n   799\t        [follower (drop-dial follower link now) (lost-reason d)]\n   800\t\n   801\t        :else [follower link nil]))))\n   802\t\n   803\t\n   804\t(defn- step-links\n   805\t  \"Step every principal's dial: `[follower links lines]`, one line per\n   806\t   change of a dial's failure, never one per attempt.\"\n   807\t  [follower node now]\n   808\t  (let [{:keys [sources links]} (::follow node)]\n   809\t    (reduce (fn [[follower links lines] [p source]]\n   810\t              (let [[follower link failure] (step-link follower (::ws node)\n   811\t                                                       source\n   812\t                                                       ;; a map from the\n   813\t                                                       ;; start: on\n   814\t                                                       ;; ClojureDart an\n   815\t                                                       ;; assoc of two or more\n   816\t                                                       ;; keyword pairs is\n   817\t                                                       ;; inlined to -conj,\n   818\t                                                       ;; and -conj on nil\n   819\t                                                       ;; conses a list; the\n   820\t                                                       ;; JVM and Node make\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc | sed -n '1,420p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yin.repl.dht\n     2\t  \"The REPL's DHT index store, `--index-store dht:<dir>` (DHT epic slice\n     3\t   S5: docs/design/dao.jing.dht.md section 10; docs/design/\n     4\t   yin.repl.dao.space-index.md, \\\"DHT store\\\").  It is composed with the\n     5\t   plain Clojure path, `dao.space.dht`, and adds only what the shell owns:\n     6\t   the durable directory, the lines it prints, and when it admits\n     7\t   evaluation.\n     8\t\n     9\t   `open` opens `<dir>` exactly as `file:<dir>` does: the exclusive lock,\n    10\t   the content log, HEAD, the validated snapshot (dao.space.store), and\n    11\t   joins a `dao.space.dht` node with that locked store as its `:local`.\n    12\t   The indexer publishes through the node's store: each put inserts\n    13\t   locally and appends one replicate request, and the manifest reads back\n    14\t   locally, so a round never waits on the network.  The HEAD write then\n    15\t   announces the publication to the node.\n    16\t\n    17\t   `step` is the node's one step owner, called by the host's single\n    18\t   ticker (yin.repl.main/step-all) with the host's clock reading; it\n    19\t   renders the node's events as the lines the REPL prints: where the\n    20\t   socket bound, and for each publication its result (acknowledged,\n    21\t   sent to N peers, or partial or not acknowledged with the count of\n    22\t   blobs not sent, the first reason, and whether the node is retrying)\n    23\t   and each later change of it (yin.vm.linker.dht.md 5.5.6).  A load's\n    24\t   failure reason is data; it is rendered as text here.\n    25\t\n    26\t   A reader handed a manifest address (`:manifest`, a pin) loads it\n    27\t   through `dao.space.dht/load-index` before the shell admits any\n    28\t   evaluation, as a restart installs its recovery first, then writes it\n    29\t   to HEAD and rehydrates the indexer from the loaded datoms, so `q`\n    30\t   answers the remote run's facts.  A load that cannot complete, or a\n    31\t   socket that cannot bind, refuses the shell (`refusal`); it never\n    32\t   starts over an empty index.  Remote indexes are also reachable at the\n    33\t   prompt, through the `dao.space.dht` host module (yin.repl.query), over\n    34\t   the same node.\n    35\t\n    36\t   The published head trace (docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.head.md,\n    37\t   slice H3) is composed here too, the shell owning the file, the lines\n    38\t   and the dial:\n    39\t   * A publisher (a key, a socket and `:publish?`) deposits its HEAD's\n    40\t     trace on its board (`yin.vm.linker.head/deposit!`) at every HEAD\n    41\t     write, after `announce!`, at startup for a recovered HEAD, and once\n    42\t     when a hydration completes (5.4).  Once its socket is bound on a\n    43\t     loopback literal it serves the board at the same port number\n    44\t     (`yin.vm.linker.head.board/serve`) and prints the join\n    45\t     token `yin:<host:port>/<principal>` when that endpoint is bound.\n    46\t   * A reader (`:follow`, each `{:principal hex :host h :port p}` with a\n    47\t     loopback host) restores `<dir>/heads.edn` before any connection\n    48\t     (5.7), dials each principal's board at the address it was given and\n    49\t     nowhere else, steps the follower after the node, and installs a\n    50\t     confirmed head only after `heads.edn` holds it.\"\n    51\t  (:require #?(:cljd [clojure.edn :as edn]\n    52\t               :clj [clojure.edn :as edn]\n    53\t               :cljs [cljs.reader :as reader])\n    54\t            [clojure.string :as str]\n    55\t            [dao.space.dht :as dht]\n    56\t            [dao.space.index :as space.index]\n    57\t            [dao.space.store :as durable]\n    58\t            [dao.space.store.fs :as fs]\n    59\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n    60\t            [dao.stream.remote-channel :as remote-channel]\n    61\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ringbuffer]\n    62\t            [yin.repl.connect :as connect]\n    63\t            [yin.repl.index :as index]\n    64\t            [yin.repl.store :as store]\n    65\t            [yin.vm.linker.dht :as ld]\n    66\t            [yin.vm.linker.head :as head]\n    67\t            [yin.vm.linker.head.board :as head.board]\n    68\t            [yin.vm.linker.interpreter :as link]\n    69\t            [yin.vm.linker.sign :as sign]\n    70\t            [yin.vm.module :as module]))\n    71\t\n    72\t\n    73\t(def default-max-inbound-bytes\n    74\t  \"The CLI default of the inbound storage bound; `dao.space.dht`'s.\"\n    75\t  dht/default-max-inbound-bytes)\n    76\t\n    77\t\n    78\t(def heads-file\n    79\t  \"The follower's durable state in the store directory (5.7).\"\n    80\t  \"heads.edn\")\n    81\t\n    82\t\n    83\t(def heads-max-bytes\n    84\t  \"The most bytes a `heads.edn` may hold: 64 followed principals take a\n    85\t   few tens of KiB, so a larger file is refused before it is decoded.\"\n    86\t  (* 1024 1024))\n    87\t\n    88\t\n    89\t(defn- refused-head\n    90\t  \"Why a reader cannot hydrate `manifest` into a directory whose own HEAD\n    91\t   already names `recovered`, or nil.  Hydration never replaces an index\n    92\t   the directory holds.\"\n    93\t  [dir manifest recovered]\n    94\t  (when (and manifest recovered (not= manifest recovered))\n    95\t    (str dir \" already holds an index (HEAD names \" recovered \"); hydrate \"\n    96\t         manifest \" into an empty directory\")))\n    97\t\n    98\t\n    99\t;; =============================================================================\n   100\t;; heads.edn (5.7)\n   101\t;; =============================================================================\n   102\t\n   103\t(defn- read-edn\n   104\t  [text]\n   105\t  #?(:cljd (edn/read-string text)\n   106\t     :clj (edn/read-string text)\n   107\t     :cljs (reader/read-string text)))\n   108\t\n   109\t\n   110\t(defn- read-one\n   111\t  \"The one EDN form `text` holds, or ::unreadable: a trailing form, a\n   112\t   truncated suffix and an empty text are refused, as on every host's\n   113\t   `read-string` alone they are not.  The text is read inside a vector\n   114\t   closed by a sentinel no file can predict, so the first form that\n   115\t   reads is the whole vector only when the text is exactly one complete\n   116\t   form (whitespace and comments around it allowed).\"\n   117\t  [text]\n   118\t  (let [end (keyword \"yin.repl.dht\" (str \"end-\" (random-uuid)))\n   119\t        ;; a newline ends a trailing comment; no whitespace precedes the\n   120\t        ;; closer (ClojureDart's reader refuses one)\n   121\t        forms (read-edn (str \"[\" text \"\\n\" end \"]\"))]\n   122\t    (if (and (vector? forms) (= 2 (count forms)) (= end (second forms)))\n   123\t      (first forms)\n   124\t      ::unreadable)))\n   125\t\n   126\t\n   127\t(defn parse-heads\n   128\t  \"The records `text`, a `heads.edn` read from `path`, holds:\n   129\t   `{:records {:version 1 :heads {principal trace}}}`, or `{:refusal\n   130\t   text}` when it is not exactly one readable EDN form or not a version-1\n   131\t   heads file.\n   132\t   Never throws.  The records themselves are verified by\n   133\t   `yin.vm.linker.head/follow`.\"\n   134\t  [path text]\n   135\t  (let [data (try (read-one text)\n   136\t                  (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n   137\t                    ::unreadable))]\n   138\t    (cond\n   139\t      (= ::unreadable data)\n   140\t      {:refusal (str \"heads file \" path \": it is not readable EDN\")}\n   141\t\n   142\t      (not (and (map? data) (= 1 (:version data)) (map? (:heads data))\n   143\t                (= #{:version :heads} (set (keys data)))))\n   144\t      {:refusal (str \"heads file \" path \": it is not a version-1 heads file\")}\n   145\t\n   146\t      :else {:records data})))\n   147\t\n   148\t\n   149\t(defn render-heads\n   150\t  \"The text of `records`: one EDN map, with no whitespace before a\n   151\t   closing bracket (ClojureDart's reader refuses one).\"\n   152\t  [records]\n   153\t  (str (pr-str records) \"\\n\"))\n   154\t\n   155\t\n   156\t(defn- without-boms\n   157\t  \"`text` without its leading byte order marks, every one of them: one\n   158\t   policy on every host, whose decoders differ (Node's drops one, the\n   159\t   JVM's keeps U+FEFF).  The run is scanned by index and cut once, so a\n   160\t   file of marks costs one pass, not one copy per mark.\"\n   161\t  [text]\n   162\t  (let [n (count text)\n   163\t        i (loop [i 0]\n   164\t            (if (and (< i n) (= \"\\uFEFF\" (subs text i (inc i))))\n   165\t              (recur (inc i))\n   166\t              i))]\n   167\t    (if (zero? i) text (subs text i))))\n   168\t\n   169\t\n   170\t(defn read-heads\n   171\t  \"The persisted head records of the store directory `dir`: `{:records\n   172\t   r}`, an empty version-1 record when no `heads.edn` exists, or\n   173\t   `{:refusal text}`: a file that cannot be read, holds more than\n   174\t   `heads-max-bytes`, is not valid UTF-8, holds a byte order mark\n   175\t   anywhere but at its start, or is not exactly one version-1 record.\n   176\t   Never throws.\"\n   177\t  [dir]\n   178\t  (let [path (str dir \"/\" heads-file)\n   179\t        bs (try (fs/read-bounded path heads-max-bytes)\n   180\t                (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n   181\t                  {::failed (or (ex-message e) (str e))}))\n   182\t        text (when (and (some? bs) (not (map? bs))\n   183\t                        (<= (fs/byte-length bs) heads-max-bytes))\n   184\t               (try (fs/decode-utf8 bs)\n   185\t                    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n   186\t                      ::invalid)))\n   187\t        body (when (string? text) (without-boms text))]\n   188\t    (cond\n   189\t      (nil? bs) {:records {:version 1 :heads {}}}\n   190\t      (map? bs) {:refusal (str \"heads file \" path \": it cannot be read (\"\n   191\t                               (::failed bs) \")\")}\n   192\t      (nil? text) {:refusal (str \"heads file \" path \": it holds more than \"\n   193\t                                 heads-max-bytes \" bytes\")}\n   194\t      (= ::invalid text) {:refusal (str \"heads file \" path\n   195\t                                        \": it is not valid UTF-8\")}\n   196\t      ;; a mark past the leading run is refused before the reader sees\n   197\t      ;; it: one host's reader takes it for whitespace, another's for a\n   198\t      ;; token, and a record never holds one\n   199\t      (str/includes? body \"\\uFEFF\")\n   200\t      {:refusal (str \"heads file \" path \": it is not valid: a byte order \"\n   201\t                     \"mark (U+FEFF) follows its start\")}\n   202\t\n   203\t      :else (parse-heads path body))))\n   204\t\n   205\t\n   206\t;; =============================================================================\n   207\t;; The board and the deposit (5.4)\n   208\t;; =============================================================================\n   209\t\n   210\t(defn- ring\n   211\t  [n]\n   212\t  (:dao.stream/handle\n   213\t    (ringbuffer/create! {:dao.stream/type ringbuffer/transport-type\n   214\t                         ringbuffer/capacity-key n})))\n   215\t\n   216\t\n   217\t(defn- deposit-head!\n   218\t  \"Deposit the trace of `manifest`, read from `store`, on `board`; a\n   219\t   refusal is appended to `notes` for the step to print.\"\n   220\t  [{:keys [board key dht-store notes]} manifest]\n   221\t  (let [r (try (head/deposit! board key manifest\n   222\t                              (space.index/read-datoms dht-store manifest))\n   223\t               (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n   224\t                 {:status :refused :reason :yin.head/unreadable\n   225\t                  :manifest manifest :detail (or (ex-message e) (str e))}))]\n   226\t    (when (= :refused (:status r))\n   227\t      (stream/append! notes r))\n   228\t    r))\n   229\t\n   230\t\n   231\t(defn- publisher\n   232\t  \"The board composition of a publishing node: a key, a socket (peers)\n   233\t   and `:publish?` (5.4), or nil.\"\n   234\t  [{:keys [peers publish?]} key base]\n   235\t  (when (and (map? key) (:seed key) (:public key) publish? (seq peers))\n   236\t    (let [notes (ring 64)]\n   237\t      {:board (head/board!)\n   238\t       :key key\n   239\t       :principal (sign/principal (:public key))\n   240\t       :dht-store base\n   241\t       :notes notes\n   242\t       :notes-cursor (:dao.stream/cursor\n   243\t                       (stream/cursor notes stream/anchor-newest))})))\n   244\t\n   245\t\n   246\t;; =============================================================================\n   247\t;; Opening the store\n   248\t;; =============================================================================\n   249\t\n   250\t(defn followed-principals\n   251\t  \"The principal ids, `ed25519:<hex>`, a DHT store spec follows.\"\n   252\t  [spec]\n   253\t  (mapv #(sign/principal (:principal %)) (:follow spec)))\n   254\t\n   255\t\n   256\t(defn- checked-follow\n   257\t  \"The `:follow` entries of `spec`, each `{:principal hex :host h :port\n   258\t   p}` with a loopback literal host, one per principal; throws a refusal\n   259\t   otherwise.\"\n   260\t  [{:keys [follow peers]}]\n   261\t  (let [refuse #(throw (ex-info % {:follow follow}))]\n   262\t    (when-not (or (nil? follow) (vector? follow))\n   263\t      (refuse \"the followed principals must be a vector\"))\n   264\t    (doseq [{:keys [principal host port] :as f} follow]\n   265\t      (when-not (and (map? f) (string? principal)\n   266\t                     (re-matches #\"[0-9a-f]{64}\" principal))\n   267\t        (refuse (str \"--dht-follow names a principal by 64 lowercase \"\n   268\t                     \"hexadecimal characters, not \" (pr-str principal))))\n   269\t      (when-not (remote-channel/loopback-literal? host)\n   270\t        (refuse (str \"--dht-follow \" principal \"@\" host \":\" port\n   271\t                     \": the head board is followed on loopback only\")))\n   272\t      (when-not (and (integer? port) (<= 1 port 65535))\n   273\t        (refuse (str \"--dht-follow \" principal \": the port must be 1 to \"\n   274\t                     \"65535, not \" (pr-str port)))))\n   275\t    (when (and (seq follow) (empty? peers))\n   276\t      (refuse (str \"--dht-follow needs a --dht-peer: a followed head's \"\n   277\t                   \"index is fetched over the DHT\")))\n   278\t    (when-not (= (count follow) (count (distinct (map :principal follow))))\n   279\t      (refuse \"--dht-follow names each principal once: one source each\"))\n   280\t    (vec follow)))\n   281\t\n   282\t\n   283\t(defn- heads-records\n   284\t  \"The records of `<dir>/heads.edn` when `follow` is not empty, read\n   285\t   before the node binds anything; a file that cannot be read as one\n   286\t   version-1 record refuses startup naming it.\"\n   287\t  [dir follow]\n   288\t  (when (seq follow)\n   289\t    (let [{:keys [records refusal]} (read-heads dir)]\n   290\t      (when refusal\n   291\t        (throw (ex-info (str refusal \"; move it aside to follow every \"\n   292\t                             \"principal from no head, dropping each one's \"\n   293\t                             \"rollback floor until a head is installed\")\n   294\t                        {:dir dir})))\n   295\t      records)))\n   296\t\n   297\t\n   298\t(defn- follower-of\n   299\t  \"The follower of `follow` on `node`, restored from the persisted\n   300\t   `records` before any connection: `[follower node]`, or `[nil node]`\n   301\t   when nothing is followed.  A record that fails refuses startup naming\n   302\t   it.\"\n   303\t  [node dir follow records]\n   304\t  (if (empty? follow)\n   305\t    [nil node]\n   306\t    (let [path (str dir \"/\" heads-file)]\n   307\t      (try\n   308\t        (head/follow node {:follow (mapv #(sign/principal (:principal %))\n   309\t                                         follow)\n   310\t                           :heads records})\n   311\t        (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n   312\t          (if-some [reason (:yin.head/refused (ex-data e))]\n   313\t            (throw (ex-info (str \"heads file \" path \": \" (ex-message e)\n   314\t                                 \" (\" reason \"); remove that record to \"\n   315\t                                 \"follow it from no head, dropping its \"\n   316\t                                 \"rollback floor until a head is installed\")\n   317\t                            {:dir dir :reason reason}))\n   318\t            (throw e)))))))\n   319\t\n   320\t\n   321\t(defn- compose\n   322\t  \"The store handle of `open`, over the joined `node`: the publisher's\n   323\t   board, the follower restored from `records`, a pinned hydration, and\n   324\t   the HEAD write that announces and deposits.\"\n   325\t  [node base {:keys [dir manifest] :as checked} follow records\n   326\t   {:keys [key ws write-heads!]}]\n   327\t  (let [pub (publisher checked key base)\n   328\t        [follower node] (follower-of node dir follow records)\n   329\t        node (cond-> (assoc node ::dir dir ::ws ws)\n   330\t               pub (assoc ::publisher pub)\n   331\t               follower (assoc ::follower follower\n   332\t                               ::follow\n   333\t                               {:sources (into {}\n   334\t                                               (map (fn [f]\n   335\t                                                      [(sign/principal\n   336\t                                                         (:principal f))\n   337\t                                                       f]))\n   338\t                                               follow)\n   339\t                                :links {}\n   340\t                                :waiting {}\n   341\t                                :write! (or write-heads! fs/atomic-replace!)})\n   342\t               (and manifest (not= manifest (get-in base [:recovery\n   343\t                                                          :manifest])))\n   344\t               (-> (dht/load-index manifest)\n   345\t                   (assoc ::hydrating manifest)))]\n   346\t    ;; a recovered HEAD's trace, so a reader's first contact needs no new\n   347\t    ;; round (5.4)\n   348\t    (when-some [recovered (and pub (get-in base [:recovery :manifest]))]\n   349\t      (deposit-head! pub recovered))\n   350\t    (assoc (dht/store node)\n   351\t           :head-fn (fn [manifest-address]\n   352\t                      ((:head-fn base) manifest-address)\n   353\t                      (dht/announce! node manifest-address)\n   354\t                      (when pub (deposit-head! pub manifest-address)))\n   355\t           :recovery (:recovery base)\n   356\t           :durable-dir dir\n   357\t           :dht node)))\n   358\t\n   359\t\n   360\t(defn- quietly!\n   361\t  \"Run the cleanup `f`, swallowing what it throws: a cleanup never\n   362\t   replaces the refusal that caused it.\"\n   363\t  [f]\n   364\t  (try (f) nil\n   365\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil)))\n   366\t\n   367\t\n   368\t(defn open\n   369\t  \"Open a `dht:<dir>` store from its spec (yin.repl.store/checked-spec):\n   370\t   the durable directory store, and the `dao.space.dht` node joined over\n   371\t   it.  Answers the store handle the shell keeps (the node's store, with\n   372\t   the durable HEAD write announcing each publication, the recovery, and\n   373\t   the directory), carrying the node under `:dht`, which the shell moves\n   374\t   onto its own state (yin.repl/create-state).\n   375\t\n   376\t   `opts`: `:key`, the publisher key `{:seed :public}`, which makes a\n   377\t   publishing node deposit its head; `:ws`, the host WebSocket seam\n   378\t   `{:connect! :bind! :unbind!}` (yin.repl.host) the board is served and\n   379\t   dialed over; `:write-heads!`, `(fn [dir name text])`, the atomic file\n   380\t   replace `heads.edn` is written with (`dao.space.store.fs` by\n   381\t   default); `:open-store`, `(fn [dir])`, the durable directory open\n   382\t   (`dao.space.store/open` by default).\n   383\t\n   384\t   A refusal releases everything it opened, exactly once, and is\n   385\t   answered as itself whatever the release throws: before the join the\n   386\t   directory store is closed; once joined the node owns it, and closing\n   387\t   the node closes the socket and then the store.\"\n   388\t  ([spec] (open spec {}))\n   389\t  ([spec {:keys [key ws write-heads! open-store]}]\n   390\t   (let [{:keys [dir peers publish? bind-host bind-port max-inbound-bytes\n   391\t                 manifest bind!]\n   392\t          :as checked} (store/checked-spec spec)\n   393\t         follow (checked-follow checked)\n   394\t         base ((or open-store durable/open) dir)\n   395\t         [node records]\n   396\t         (try\n   397\t           (when-some [why (refused-head dir manifest\n   398\t                                         (get-in base [:recovery :manifest]))]\n   399\t             (throw (ex-info why {:dir dir :manifest manifest})))\n   400\t           (let [records (heads-records dir follow)]\n   401\t             [(dht/join {:local base\n   402\t                         :peers peers\n   403\t                         :publish? publish?\n   404\t                         :bind-host bind-host\n   405\t                         :bind-port bind-port\n   406\t                         :max-inbound-bytes max-inbound-bytes\n   407\t                         :bind! (or bind! (dht/default-bind))})\n   408\t              records])\n   409\t           (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n   410\t             (quietly! #(store/close! base))\n   411\t             (throw e)))]\n   412\t     ;; from here the node owns the store and holds a socket\n   413\t     (try\n   414\t       (compose node base checked follow records\n   415\t                {:key key :ws ws :write-heads! write-heads!})\n   416\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n   417\t         (quietly! #(dht/close! node))\n   418\t         (throw e))))))\n   419\t\n   420\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc | sed -n '821,1145p'\"","aggregated_output":"   821\t                                                       ;; a map\n   822\t                                                       (get links p {})\n   823\t                                                       now)\n   824\t                    fresh? (and failure (not= failure (:failed (get links p))))]\n   825\t                [follower\n   826\t                 (assoc links p (cond-> link failure (assoc :failed failure)))\n   827\t                 (cond-> lines fresh? (conj (dial-line p source failure)))]))\n   828\t            [follower links []]\n   829\t            sources)))\n   830\t\n   831\t\n   832\t(defn- persist\n   833\t  \"5.7 steps 2 and 3 for `principal`'s confirmed `trace`: replace\n   834\t   `heads.edn` with it in its place, and only when that returned,\n   835\t   install it.  A write that fails installs nothing and waits for the\n   836\t   repair delay.  Answers `[follower node waiting events]`.\"\n   837\t  [follower node waiting principal trace now]\n   838\t  (let [{:keys [write!]} (::follow node)\n   839\t        dir (::dir node)\n   840\t        failed (try (write! dir heads-file\n   841\t                            (render-heads (head/records follower principal\n   842\t                                                        trace)))\n   843\t                    nil\n   844\t                    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n   845\t                      (or (ex-message e) (str e))))]\n   846\t    (if failed\n   847\t      (let [delay (next-delay follower (get-in waiting [principal :delay]))]\n   848\t        [follower node\n   849\t         (assoc waiting principal {:trace trace :due (+ now delay)\n   850\t                                   :delay delay})\n   851\t         [{:yin.head/event :unpersisted :principal principal :trace trace\n   852\t           :detail failed :delay delay}]])\n   853\t      (let [[follower node events] (head/install follower node principal\n   854\t                                                 trace)]\n   855\t        [follower node (dissoc waiting principal) events]))))\n   856\t\n   857\t\n   858\t(defn- retry-waiting\n   859\t  \"Write again each confirmed head whose write failed, once its delay\n   860\t   has passed and while it is still the principal's confirmed candidate.\"\n   861\t  [follower node waiting now]\n   862\t  (reduce (fn [[follower node waiting events] [p {:keys [trace due]}]]\n   863\t            (let [cand (get-in (head/heads follower) [p :candidate])]\n   864\t              (cond\n   865\t                (not (and (= :confirmed (:state cand)) (= trace (:trace cand))))\n   866\t                [follower node (dissoc waiting p) events]\n   867\t\n   868\t                (< now due) [follower node waiting events]\n   869\t\n   870\t                :else\n   871\t                (let [[follower node waiting more]\n   872\t                      (persist follower node waiting p trace now)]\n   873\t                  [follower node waiting (into events more)]))))\n   874\t          [follower node waiting []]\n   875\t          waiting))\n   876\t\n   877\t\n   878\t(defn linked-registry\n   879\t  \"`{name manifest-address}` of the modules a VM module `registry` holds\n   880\t   linked through the linker: a linked entry carries its manifest's\n   881\t   address, a host module none.\"\n   882\t  [registry]\n   883\t  (into {}\n   884\t        (keep (fn [[n e]] (when (some? (:address e)) [n (:address e)])))\n   885\t        (module/module-entries registry)))\n   886\t\n   887\t\n   888\t(defn moved\n   889\t  \"The linked names of the shell's session whose resolved address\n   890\t   differs now (`yin.vm.linker.head/moved`): derived, stored nowhere.\"\n   891\t  [shell node]\n   892\t  (head/moved (ld/names node (link/authority (:link-source shell)))\n   893\t              (linked-registry (get-in shell [:vm :modules]))))\n   894\t\n   895\t\n   896\t(defn- movers\n   897\t  \"Of `installed`, this step's install events, those whose install moved\n   898\t   each name of `moves` to where it resolves now in `node`, `{name\n   899\t   [event]}`: an install moved a name when, with only that principal's\n   900\t   head put back where it stood in `before`, the name resolves elsewhere\n   901\t   or not at all.  Derived from the two nodes, stored nowhere.  One\n   902\t   install moved every name; a name no single install accounts for is\n   903\t   given every install.\"\n   904\t  [shell before node installed moves]\n   905\t  (if (< (count installed) 2)\n   906\t    (into {} (map (fn [m] [(:name m) installed])) moves)\n   907\t    (let [authority (link/authority (:link-source shell))\n   908\t          without (fn [{:keys [principal]}]\n   909\t                    (let [put-back (get-in before [ld/installed-key principal])]\n   910\t                      (:names (ld/names\n   911\t                                (if (some? put-back)\n   912\t                                  (assoc-in node [ld/installed-key principal]\n   913\t                                            put-back)\n   914\t                                  (update node ld/installed-key dissoc\n   915\t                                          principal))\n   916\t                                authority))))\n   917\t          envs (mapv without installed)]\n   918\t      (into {}\n   919\t            (map (fn [{n :name :keys [resolved]}]\n   920\t                   (let [mine (into []\n   921\t                                    (keep-indexed\n   922\t                                      (fn [i e]\n   923\t                                        (let [entry (get (nth envs i) n)]\n   924\t                                          (when-not (and (= :ok (:status entry))\n   925\t                                                         (= resolved\n   926\t                                                            (:address entry)))\n   927\t                                            e))))\n   928\t                                    installed)]\n   929\t                     [n (if (seq mine) mine installed)])))\n   930\t            moves))))\n   931\t\n   932\t\n   933\t(defn moved-lines\n   934\t  \"The line of 5.7 for each linked name an installed head moved, naming\n   935\t   the head of the principal whose install moved it (`movers`): only\n   936\t   moves that were not already standing before this step's installs\n   937\t   (`before`, the node then), so a name is reported once per new\n   938\t   address, and nothing is stored.  `installed` is the step's\n   939\t   `:installed` events.\"\n   940\t  [shell before node installed]\n   941\t  (when (seq installed)\n   942\t    (let [standing (set (map (juxt :name :resolved) (moved shell before)))\n   943\t          moves (into []\n   944\t                      (remove #(contains? standing [(:name %) (:resolved %)]))\n   945\t                      (moved shell node))\n   946\t          by-name (movers shell before node installed moves)]\n   947\t      (mapv (fn [{n :name :keys [linked resolved]}]\n   948\t              (str \"dht: \" n \" moved: linked \" linked\n   949\t                   \", now resolves to \" resolved \" (head of \"\n   950\t                   (str/join \", \"\n   951\t                             (map (fn [{:keys [principal trace]}]\n   952\t                                    (str principal \" seq \"\n   953\t                                         (get-in trace [:yin.head/envelope\n   954\t                                                        :yin.head/seq])))\n   955\t                                  (get by-name n)))\n   956\t                   \"); (reset) then (require '\" n \") links it\"))\n   957\t            moves))))\n   958\t\n   959\t\n   960\t(defn- step-follow\n   961\t  \"One pass of the follower after the node: dials, `head/step`, and for\n   962\t   each confirmed head the write that precedes its install.  Answers\n   963\t   `[node lines events]`.\"\n   964\t  [shell node now]\n   965\t  (if-some [follower (::follower node)]\n   966\t    (let [before node\n   967\t          ;; a stopping node composes and steps no dial\n   968\t          [follower links dial-lines] (if (::stopping? node)\n   969\t                                        [follower (get-in node [::follow :links]) []]\n   970\t                                        (step-links follower node now))\n   971\t          [follower node events] (head/step follower node now)\n   972\t          ;; a lost source: drop its dial; the next is composed after the\n   973\t          ;; delay, and the follower mints :oldest on its handle.  A\n   974\t          ;; stopping node schedules none.\n   975\t          links (if (::stopping? node)\n   976\t                  links\n   977\t                  (reduce (fn [links {:keys [principal]}]\n   978\t                            (update links principal\n   979\t                                    #(drop-dial follower % now)))\n   980\t                          links\n   981\t                          (filter #(= :source-lost (:yin.head/event %)) events)))\n   982\t          waiting (get-in node [::follow :waiting])\n   983\t          [follower node waiting retried] (retry-waiting follower node waiting\n   984\t                                                         now)\n   985\t          [follower node waiting persisted]\n   986\t          (reduce (fn [[follower node waiting more] {:keys [principal trace]}]\n   987\t                    (let [[follower node waiting es]\n   988\t                          (persist follower node waiting principal trace now)]\n   989\t                      [follower node waiting (into more es)]))\n   990\t                  [follower node waiting []]\n   991\t                  (filter #(= :confirmed (:yin.head/event %)) events))\n   992\t          events (-> events (into retried) (into persisted))\n   993\t          node (-> node\n   994\t                   (assoc ::follower follower)\n   995\t                   (update ::follow assoc :links links :waiting waiting))\n   996\t          installed (filterv #(= :installed (:yin.head/event %)) events)]\n   997\t      [node\n   998\t       (-> dial-lines\n   999\t           (into (keep head-line) events)\n  1000\t           (into (moved-lines shell before node installed)))\n  1001\t       events])\n  1002\t    [node [] []]))\n  1003\t\n  1004\t\n  1005\t;; =============================================================================\n  1006\t;; The step\n  1007\t;; =============================================================================\n  1008\t\n  1009\t(defn step\n  1010\t  \"Advance the shell's node once at the host's clock reading `now`\n  1011\t   (dao.space.dht/step) and answer `[shell' lines events]`: its events as\n  1012\t   lines, and as the data the ticker reads to re-check a pending require\n  1013\t   (yin.repl/recheck-on-tick), a completed hydration installed, a\n  1014\t   failed one or a failed bind recorded as the shell's refusal.  The\n  1015\t   head composition steps after the node: the board's endpoint (and the\n  1016\t   join token once it is bound), then the follower, whose events join\n  1017\t   the node's.  A shell without a DHT store is answered unchanged.\"\n  1018\t  [shell now]\n  1019\t  (if-let\n  1020\t    [node (:dht shell)]\n  1021\t    (let\n  1022\t      [[node events] (dht/step node now)\n  1023\t       node (assoc node ::now now)\n  1024\t       node (reduce (fn [node {:keys [host port], :as event}]\n  1025\t                      (cond-> node\n  1026\t                        (= :bound (::dht/event event))\n  1027\t                        (assoc ::listen [host port])))\n  1028\t                    node\n  1029\t                    events)\n  1030\t       lines (mapv #(event-line node %) events)\n  1031\t       [node board-lines] (if-some [pub (::publisher node)]\n  1032\t                            (let [[pub ls] (step-board pub node events now)]\n  1033\t                              [(assoc node ::publisher pub) ls])\n  1034\t                            [node []])\n  1035\t       [node follow-lines head-events] (step-follow shell node now)\n  1036\t       lines (-> lines (into board-lines) (into follow-lines))\n  1037\t       hydrating (::hydrating node)\n  1038\t       status (when hydrating (:status (dht/load-status node hydrating)))\n  1039\t       node (cond->\n  1040\t              node\n  1041\t              (and hydrating (= :failed status))\n  1042\t              (assoc\n  1043\t                ::refusal (str/join\n  1044\t                            \"\\n\" (filter\n  1045\t                                   #(str/includes?\n  1046\t                                      %\n  1047\t                                      \"refused\")\n  1048\t                                   lines)))\n  1049\t              (dht/refusal node)\n  1050\t              (assoc ::refusal (dht/refusal node)))\n  1051\t       shell (assoc shell :dht node)]\n  1052\t      [(if (= :loaded status) (hydrated shell node) shell)\n  1053\t       lines\n  1054\t       (into (vec events) head-events)])\n  1055\t    [shell [] []]))\n  1056\t\n  1057\t\n  1058\t(defn refusal\n  1059\t  \"The text that refused the shell's DHT store after startup (a failed\n  1060\t   bind or a hydration that could not complete), or nil.\"\n  1061\t  [shell]\n  1062\t  (get-in shell [:dht ::refusal]))\n  1063\t\n  1064\t\n  1065\t(defn admitting?\n  1066\t  \"True when the shell may evaluate: no hydration is outstanding and none\n  1067\t   was refused.  Following never holds evaluation back (5.8).\"\n  1068\t  [shell]\n  1069\t  (let [node (:dht shell)]\n  1070\t    (or (nil? node)\n  1071\t        (and (nil? (::hydrating node)) (nil? (::refusal node))))))\n  1072\t\n  1073\t\n  1074\t(defn busy?\n  1075\t  \"True while the node owes the REPL a line; the ticker keeps its base\n  1076\t   cadence then.  Following alone is never busy (section 7): only a\n  1077\t   candidate's load is, as a load of the node.\"\n  1078\t  [shell]\n  1079\t  (boolean (some-> (:dht shell) dht/busy?)))\n  1080\t\n  1081\t\n  1082\t(defn follow-lines\n  1083\t  \"What the shell states at startup per followed principal: where it is\n  1084\t   followed, and whether a head is installed (5.8).\"\n  1085\t  [shell]\n  1086\t  (let [node (:dht shell)]\n  1087\t    (when-some [follower (::follower node)]\n  1088\t      (mapv (fn [[p {:keys [manifest floor]}]]\n  1089\t              (let [{:keys [host port]} (get-in node [::follow :sources p])]\n  1090\t                (str \"dht: following \" p \" at \" (address-text host port) \"; \"\n  1091\t                     (if manifest\n  1092\t                       (str \"installed head \" manifest \" (seq \" floor \")\")\n  1093\t                       (str \"no head installed yet: a (require ...) of its \"\n  1094\t                            \"names waits for the first\")))))\n  1095\t            (head/heads follower)))))\n  1096\t\n  1097\t\n  1098\t(defn banner\n  1099\t  \"What the REPL states at startup about a DHT store spec, before the\n  1100\t   node steps once, and so before anything is shared.\"\n  1101\t  [{:keys [dir peers publish? bind-host bind-port follow-suspended]}]\n  1102\t  (let [content (durable/content-path dir)\n  1103\t        peers-text (str/join \", \" (map #(address-text (:host %) (:port %))\n  1104\t                                       peers))]\n  1105\t    (cond-> []\n  1106\t      (empty? peers)\n  1107\t      (conj (str \"dht: solo, no --dht-peer, so no socket is opened; \"\n  1108\t                 \"publications are durable in \" dir\n  1109\t                 \" and acknowledged by no one\"))\n  1110\t\n  1111\t      (seq peers)\n  1112\t      (conj (str \"dht: binding \" (address-text bind-host bind-port)\n  1113\t                 (when (zero? bind-port) \" (ephemeral)\")\n  1114\t                 \"; peers \" peers-text))\n  1115\t\n  1116\t      (and publish? (seq peers))\n  1117\t      (conj (str \"dht: publishing is ON. Everything in \" content\n  1118\t                 \" will be shared: the whole code index this directory holds\"\n  1119\t                 \", every program recovered from HEAD and every program\"\n  1120\t                 \" evaluated from now on, with any peer that asks for its\"\n  1121\t                 \" address. Omit --dht-publish to fetch only.\"))\n  1122\t\n  1123\t      (and publish? (empty? peers))\n  1124\t      (conj (str \"dht: publishing is on, but solo: nothing in \" content\n  1125\t                 \" leaves this process\"))\n  1126\t\n  1127\t      (and (not publish?) (seq peers))\n  1128\t      (conj (str\n  1129\t              \"dht: fetch-only, nothing this node holds is \"\n  1130\t              \"shared (--dht-publish shares it)\"))\n  1131\t\n  1132\t      follow-suspended\n  1133\t      (conj (str \"dht: --dht-manifest pins this run: following is suspended \"\n  1134\t                 \"for this run (the saved --dht-follow is kept)\"))\n  1135\t\n  1136\t      true\n  1137\t      (conj (str \"dht: a (require ...) of a module this node does not hold \"\n  1138\t                 \"may fetch its code from peers; it stays pending until the \"\n  1139\t                 \"load ends, and (abandon) gives it up\")))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"The evidence supports separating the merge paths: transport-dependent fixes belong with the boundary refactor; independent host and runner fixes can proceed. Relocation alone, however, does not prove that ack collapse or repair starvation is fixed. I’m checking which behavior must be pinned before the move and verified afterward."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc | sed -n '368,770p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc | sed -n '368,770p'\"","aggregated_output":"   368\t(defn open\n   369\t  \"Open a `dht:<dir>` store from its spec (yin.repl.store/checked-spec):\n   370\t   the durable directory store, and the `dao.space.dht` node joined over\n   371\t   it.  Answers the store handle the shell keeps (the node's store, with\n   372\t   the durable HEAD write announcing each publication, the recovery, and\n   373\t   the directory), carrying the node under `:dht`, which the shell moves\n   374\t   onto its own state (yin.repl/create-state).\n   375\t\n   376\t   `opts`: `:key`, the publisher key `{:seed :public}`, which makes a\n   377\t   publishing node deposit its head; `:ws`, the host WebSocket seam\n   378\t   `{:connect! :bind! :unbind!}` (yin.repl.host) the board is served and\n   379\t   dialed over; `:write-heads!`, `(fn [dir name text])`, the atomic file\n   380\t   replace `heads.edn` is written with (`dao.space.store.fs` by\n   381\t   default); `:open-store`, `(fn [dir])`, the durable directory open\n   382\t   (`dao.space.store/open` by default).\n   383\t\n   384\t   A refusal releases everything it opened, exactly once, and is\n   385\t   answered as itself whatever the release throws: before the join the\n   386\t   directory store is closed; once joined the node owns it, and closing\n   387\t   the node closes the socket and then the store.\"\n   388\t  ([spec] (open spec {}))\n   389\t  ([spec {:keys [key ws write-heads! open-store]}]\n   390\t   (let [{:keys [dir peers publish? bind-host bind-port max-inbound-bytes\n   391\t                 manifest bind!]\n   392\t          :as checked} (store/checked-spec spec)\n   393\t         follow (checked-follow checked)\n   394\t         base ((or open-store durable/open) dir)\n   395\t         [node records]\n   396\t         (try\n   397\t           (when-some [why (refused-head dir manifest\n   398\t                                         (get-in base [:recovery :manifest]))]\n   399\t             (throw (ex-info why {:dir dir :manifest manifest})))\n   400\t           (let [records (heads-records dir follow)]\n   401\t             [(dht/join {:local base\n   402\t                         :peers peers\n   403\t                         :publish? publish?\n   404\t                         :bind-host bind-host\n   405\t                         :bind-port bind-port\n   406\t                         :max-inbound-bytes max-inbound-bytes\n   407\t                         :bind! (or bind! (dht/default-bind))})\n   408\t              records])\n   409\t           (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n   410\t             (quietly! #(store/close! base))\n   411\t             (throw e)))]\n   412\t     ;; from here the node owns the store and holds a socket\n   413\t     (try\n   414\t       (compose node base checked follow records\n   415\t                {:key key :ws ws :write-heads! write-heads!})\n   416\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n   417\t         (quietly! #(dht/close! node))\n   418\t         (throw e))))))\n   419\t\n   420\t\n   421\t(defn without-runner\n   422\t  \"The store handle the shell keeps: `open`'s answer without the node,\n   423\t   which the shell carries as its own `:dht`.  Any other handle is\n   424\t   answered as it is.\"\n   425\t  [handle]\n   426\t  (dissoc handle :dht))\n   427\t\n   428\t\n   429\t(defn follower\n   430\t  \"The head follower the shell's DHT `node` carries, or nil when it\n   431\t   follows nothing.\"\n   432\t  [node]\n   433\t  (get node ::follower))\n   434\t\n   435\t\n   436\t(defn stop!\n   437\t  \"Initiate the head composition's exit on the shell's node: the board's\n   438\t   server is asked to stop (`head.board/stop!`), every follow dial is\n   439\t   closed and no dial is composed again, and the node is marked\n   440\t   stopping.  Performs no other I/O; `step` completes the stop and\n   441\t   `stopped?` reports it.  A shell without a node, or already stopping,\n   442\t   is answered unchanged.  The board serves a read-only ring that stop\n   443\t   does not end, so a reader has nothing to be told but the reattachable\n   444\t   close its connection observes.\"\n   445\t  [shell]\n   446\t  (let [node (:dht shell)]\n   447\t    (if (or (nil? node) (::stopping? node))\n   448\t      shell\n   449\t      (do (doseq [[_ {:keys [dial]}] (get-in node [::follow :links])]\n   450\t            (when dial (head.board/close! dial)))\n   451\t          (assoc shell :dht\n   452\t                 (cond-> (assoc node ::stopping? true)\n   453\t                   (get-in node [::publisher :server])\n   454\t                   (update-in [::publisher :server] head.board/stop!)\n   455\t\n   456\t                   (::follow node)\n   457\t                   (assoc-in [::follow :links] {})))))))\n   458\t\n   459\t\n   460\t(defn stopped?\n   461\t  \"True when the head composition owes nothing at exit: no node, no\n   462\t   board server, or a board server that is stopped or refused.\"\n   463\t  [shell]\n   464\t  (let [server (get-in shell [:dht ::publisher :server])]\n   465\t    (or (nil? server) (head.board/stopped? server))))\n   466\t\n   467\t\n   468\t(defn close!\n   469\t  \"The last resort after the exit drain's budget\n   470\t   (`yin.repl.main/stop-ticks`): whatever the board still owes is asked\n   471\t   for once more and not awaited.  The ordinary exit is `stop!`, then\n   472\t   `step` until `stopped?`.  A shell never stopped is stopped first, so a\n   473\t   direct caller (a test, an embedder without a drain) still closes the\n   474\t   dials; the board's stopping tick runs at the node's last tick reading\n   475\t   only when the board is not already `stopped?`.\"\n   476\t  [shell]\n   477\t  (let [shell (stop! shell)\n   478\t        node (:dht shell)\n   479\t        server (get-in node [::publisher :server])]\n   480\t    (when (and server (not (head.board/stopped? server)))\n   481\t      (head.board/serve-step server (or (::now node) 0)))\n   482\t    nil))\n   483\t\n   484\t\n   485\t;; =============================================================================\n   486\t;; Lines\n   487\t;; =============================================================================\n   488\t\n   489\t(defn- address-text\n   490\t  [host port]\n   491\t  (if (str/includes? host \":\") (str \"[\" host \"]:\" port) (str host \":\" port)))\n   492\t\n   493\t\n   494\t(defn- reason-text\n   495\t  \"One blob's failure reason as the REPL prints it.\"\n   496\t  [node {:keys [reason peers]}]\n   497\t  (case reason\n   498\t    :dao.jing.dht/solo (str \"solo: no --dht-peer is configured, so nothing \"\n   499\t                            \"was sent; the index is in \" (::dir node) \" only\")\n   500\t    :dao.jing.dht/unpublished (str \"publication is off: this node fetches \"\n   501\t                                   \"only; start with --dht-publish to share\")\n   502\t    :dao.jing.dht/too-few-peers (str \"too few peers, sent to \" peers \" of \"\n   503\t                                     (dht/ack-peers node) \" before the \"\n   504\t                                     \"acknowledgement deadline\")\n   505\t    :dao.jing.dht/oversize \"a blob exceeds the DHT message bound\"\n   506\t    :dao.jing.dht/absent \"a blob was no longer in the local store\"\n   507\t    :dao.jing.dht/busy \"too many writes were pending\"\n   508\t    :dao.space.dht/backlog-full \"the replicate backlog was full\"\n   509\t    :dao.space.dht/publications-full (str \"too many publications awaited \"\n   510\t                                          \"their first report\")\n   511\t    :dao.space.dht/cancelled \"cancelled\"\n   512\t    (str reason)))\n   513\t\n   514\t\n   515\t(def ^:private ended-text\n   516\t  {:dao.space.dht/terminal \"every remaining failure is final\"\n   517\t   :dao.space.dht/cancelled \"cancelled\"\n   518\t   :dao.space.dht/displaced \"displaced by newer publications\"})\n   519\t\n   520\t\n   521\t(defn- result-text\n   522\t  \"A publication's result (yin.vm.linker.dht.md 5.5.6): when it is not\n   523\t   acknowledged, the count of failed blobs, the first reason, and whether\n   524\t   the node is retrying.\"\n   525\t  [node {:keys [result blobs peers failed repairing? ended]}]\n   526\t  (if (= :acknowledged result)\n   527\t    (str \"acknowledged: sent to \" peers \" peers\")\n   528\t    (str (if (= :partial result)\n   529\t           \"PARTIAL: the manifest was sent; \"\n   530\t           \"NOT acknowledged: \")\n   531\t         (reason-text node (first failed))\n   532\t         \"; \" (count failed) \" of \" blobs \" blobs not sent\"\n   533\t         (cond\n   534\t           repairing? \"; retrying while the node is open\"\n   535\t           ended (str \"; not retrying (\" (get ended-text ended (str ended)) \")\")\n   536\t           :else \"; not retrying\")\n   537\t         \"; the local copy is durable\")))\n   538\t\n   539\t\n   540\t(defn- failure-text\n   541\t  \"A load's failure reason, data (dao.space.dht 4.3), as text.\"\n   542\t  [{:dao.space.dht/keys [failure] :keys [address cause defect outcome]\n   543\t    :as reason}]\n   544\t  (case failure\n   545\t    :miss (str \"no peer produced \" address \" (\" (name cause) \")\")\n   546\t    :invalid (str \"the content \" (when address (str \"at \" address \" \"))\n   547\t                  \"is invalid (\" (:code defect) \")\"\n   548\t                  (when-let [text (:text defect)] (str \": \" text)))\n   549\t    :unaskable (str \"could not ask for \" address \" (\" (name outcome) \")\")\n   550\t    (pr-str (if (nil? failure) reason failure))))\n   551\t\n   552\t\n   553\t(defn- event-line\n   554\t  [node {:keys [manifest blobs host port id reason datoms fetched], :as event}]\n   555\t  (case (::dht/event event)\n   556\t    :bound (str \"dht: node \" (subs id 0 16) \" listening on \"\n   557\t                (address-text host port) \"; peers: \"\n   558\t                (str/join \", \" (map #(address-text (:host %) (:port %))\n   559\t                                    (:peers node)))\n   560\t                (if (:publish? node) \"; publishing\" \"; fetch-only\"))\n   561\t    :bind-failed (str \"dht: refused: the socket could not bind: \" reason)\n   562\t    (:published :republished)\n   563\t    (str \"dht: \" (name (::dht/event event)) \" \" manifest \" (\" blobs \" blobs), \"\n   564\t         (result-text node event))\n   565\t    :publication-unknown (str \"dht: published \" manifest\n   566\t                              \", acknowledgement unknown: facts were lost\")\n   567\t    :loaded (str (if (= manifest (::hydrating node)) \"dht: hydrated \"\n   568\t                     \"dht: loaded \")\n   569\t                 manifest \", \"\n   570\t                 (when datoms (str datoms \" datoms, \"))\n   571\t                 fetched \" blobs fetched\"\n   572\t                 (when (= manifest (::hydrating node)) \"; evaluation admitted\"))\n   573\t    :load-failed (str \"dht: \" (if (= manifest (::hydrating node)) \"refused: \"\n   574\t                                  \"\")\n   575\t                      \"loading \" manifest \" failed: \" (failure-text reason)\n   576\t                      (when (= manifest (::hydrating node))\n   577\t                        \"; the remote index was not hydrated\"))\n   578\t    (pr-str event)))\n   579\t\n   580\t\n   581\t(defn join-token\n   582\t  \"The one string a reader hands `yin-repl dht join`: the publishing\n   583\t   node's address and its principal's 64 hex digits, as\n   584\t   `yin:<host:port>/<principal>` (5.8).  It names no manifest: a reader\n   585\t   follows the head the principal publishes.\"\n   586\t  [host port principal]\n   587\t  (str \"yin:\" (address-text host port) \"/\" principal))\n   588\t\n   589\t\n   590\t(defn- trace-text\n   591\t  [trace]\n   592\t  (let [{:yin.head/keys [manifest] n :yin.head/seq} (:yin.head/envelope trace)]\n   593\t    (str manifest \" (seq \" n \")\")))\n   594\t\n   595\t\n   596\t(defn- head-line\n   597\t  \"A follower event (`yin.vm.linker.head`) as the line the REPL prints,\n   598\t   or nil.\"\n   599\t  [{:keys [principal trace reason failure outcome detail delay] :as e}]\n   600\t  (case (:yin.head/event e)\n   601\t    :installed (str \"dht: installed the head of \" principal \": \"\n   602\t                    (trace-text trace))\n   603\t    :refused (str \"dht: refused a head of \" principal \": \" reason\n   604\t                  (when (map? trace) (str \", \" (trace-text trace))))\n   605\t    :unloadable (str \"dht: the head of \" principal \" \" (trace-text trace)\n   606\t                     \" cannot load: \" (failure-text failure)\n   607\t                     \"; trying again after the repair delay\")\n   608\t    :source-lost (str \"dht: lost the head board of \" principal \" (\"\n   609\t                      (pr-str outcome) \"); dialing it again\")\n   610\t    :unpersisted (str \"dht: the head of \" principal \" \" (trace-text trace)\n   611\t                      \" is not installed: :yin.head/unpersisted (\" detail\n   612\t                      \"); writing \" heads-file \" again in \" delay \" ticks\")\n   613\t    nil))\n   614\t\n   615\t\n   616\t;; =============================================================================\n   617\t;; The board endpoint and the token (5.1, 5.8)\n   618\t;; =============================================================================\n   619\t\n   620\t(def ^:private board-codec\n   621\t  \"The head board's wire profile.\"\n   622\t  (:transit connect/codec-profiles))\n   623\t\n   624\t\n   625\t(defn- serve-board\n   626\t  \"Compose the board's endpoint once the node's socket is bound at\n   627\t   `host`:`port`: `[pub lines]`.\"\n   628\t  [pub ws host port]\n   629\t  (let [server (head.board/serve {:board (:board pub)\n   630\t                                  :principal (:principal pub)\n   631\t                                  :spec {:host host :port port}\n   632\t                                  :host ws\n   633\t                                  :codecs [board-codec]})]\n   634\t    [(assoc pub :server server :listen [host port])\n   635\t     (when (= :refused (:status server))\n   636\t       [(case (:reason server)\n   637\t          :yin.head/not-loopback\n   638\t          (str \"dht: the head board is served on loopback only; this node \"\n   639\t               \"binds \" host \", so it serves no board and prints no token\")\n   640\t          :dao.stream.remote-channel/no-transport\n   641\t          \"dht: this host has no WebSocket listener: no head board, no token\"\n   642\t          (str \"dht: the head board could not bind TCP \"\n   643\t               (address-text host port) \": no board, no join token; \"\n   644\t               \"choose another --dht-port\"))])]))\n   645\t\n   646\t\n   647\t(defn- stopped-line\n   648\t  \"The board's end, printed once on its transition to stopped.\"\n   649\t  [outcome]\n   650\t  (if (= :confirmed outcome)\n   651\t    \"dht: the head board stopped\"\n   652\t    (str \"dht: the head board stopped without host completion (\"\n   653\t         (name outcome) \")\")))\n   654\t\n   655\t\n   656\t(defn- step-board\n   657\t  \"Advance the board's endpoint, print the token once when it is bound,\n   658\t   the board's end once when it stops, and each deposit refusal:\n   659\t   `[pub lines]`.  A stopping node composes no board.\"\n   660\t  [pub node events now]\n   661\t  (let [bound (some #(when (= :bound (::dht/event %)) %) events)\n   662\t        [pub lines] (if (and bound (nil? (:server pub)) (not (::stopping? node)))\n   663\t                      (serve-board pub (::ws node) (:host bound) (:port bound))\n   664\t                      [pub nil])\n   665\t        before (get-in pub [:server :status])\n   666\t        server (when (:server pub) (head.board/serve-step (:server pub) now))\n   667\t        pub (cond-> pub server (assoc :server server))\n   668\t        [host port] (:listen pub)\n   669\t        lines (cond-> (vec lines)\n   670\t                (and (= :serving (:status server)) (not (:token? pub)))\n   671\t                (conj (str \"dht: join token: \"\n   672\t                           (join-token host port (:public (:key pub)))))\n   673\t\n   674\t                (and (= :refused (:status server)) (not= :refused before))\n   675\t                (conj (str \"dht: the head board could not bind TCP \"\n   676\t                           (address-text host port) \": no board, no join \"\n   677\t                           \"token; choose another --dht-port\"))\n   678\t\n   679\t                (and (= :stopped (:status server)) (not= :stopped before))\n   680\t                (conj (stopped-line (get-in server [:stop :outcome]))))\n   681\t        pub (cond-> pub (= :serving (:status server)) (assoc :token? true))\n   682\t        ;; a gap means refusals were evicted unread: adopt its recovery\n   683\t        ;; cursor, say so, and drain what the ring still holds\n   684\t        [notes lost? cursor] (loop [notes [] lost? false\n   685\t                                    cursor (:notes-cursor pub)]\n   686\t                               (let [r (stream/next (:notes pub) cursor)]\n   687\t                                 (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\n   688\t                                   :dao.stream/ok (recur (conj notes\n   689\t                                                               (:dao.stream/value r))\n   690\t                                                         lost?\n   691\t                                                         (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n   692\t                                   :dao.stream/gap (recur notes true\n   693\t                                                          (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n   694\t                                   [notes lost? cursor])))]\n   695\t    [(assoc pub :notes-cursor cursor)\n   696\t     (-> lines\n   697\t         (cond-> lost? (conj (str \"dht: more head trace refusals arrived \"\n   698\t                                  \"than could be kept; the oldest were not \"\n   699\t                                  \"reported\")))\n   700\t         (into (map (fn [{:keys [reason manifest]}]\n   701\t                      (str \"dht: the head trace of \" manifest \" was not \"\n   702\t                           \"deposited: \" reason)))\n   703\t               notes))]))\n   704\t\n   705\t\n   706\t(defn- hydrated\n   707\t  \"Install the loaded remote index as this directory's: HEAD first, then\n   708\t   the indexer, exactly as a restart's recovery is installed.  A\n   709\t   publisher deposits the hydrated HEAD's trace once (5.4).\"\n   710\t  [shell node]\n   711\t  (let [manifest (::hydrating node)\n   712\t        recovery {:manifest manifest :datoms (dht/loaded-datoms node manifest)}]\n   713\t    ((:head-fn (dht/local node)) manifest)\n   714\t    (when-some [pub (::publisher node)]\n   715\t      (deposit-head! pub manifest))\n   716\t    (-> shell\n   717\t        (update :indexer index/rehydrate recovery)\n   718\t        (assoc :index-recovery recovery\n   719\t               :dht (dissoc node ::hydrating)))))\n   720\t\n   721\t\n   722\t;; =============================================================================\n   723\t;; Following (5.3, 5.5, 5.7)\n   724\t;; =============================================================================\n   725\t\n   726\t(defn- next-delay\n   727\t  [follower delay]\n   728\t  (if delay\n   729\t    (min (* 2 delay) (:repair-max-ticks follower))\n   730\t    (:repair-ticks follower)))\n   731\t\n   732\t\n   733\t(defn- drop-dial\n   734\t  \"Close the dial of a link and schedule the next one after its delay;\n   735\t   the last failure reported is kept.\"\n   736\t  [follower link now]\n   737\t  (when-some [d (:dial link)] (head.board/close! d))\n   738\t  (let [delay (next-delay follower (:delay link))]\n   739\t    {:due (+ now delay) :delay delay :failed (:failed link)}))\n   740\t\n   741\t\n   742\t(defn- lost-reason\n   743\t  \"What ended a lost dial, as one keyword: the remote's reason, or the\n   744\t   outcome.\"\n   745\t  [d]\n   746\t  (let [o (:outcome d)]\n   747\t    (or (:dao.stream.remote/reason o) (:dao.stream/outcome o) :lost)))\n   748\t\n   749\t\n   750\t(defn- dial-line\n   751\t  \"The line a dial failure prints when it differs from the last one.\"\n   752\t  [principal {:keys [host port]} failure]\n   753\t  (str \"dht: cannot follow \" principal \" at \" (address-text host port) \": \"\n   754\t       (case failure\n   755\t         :dao.stream.remote/not-found\n   756\t         \"that endpoint serves no head board for this principal\"\n   757\t         :dao.stream.remote/channel-gone\n   758\t         \"the connection was refused, closed, or stopped answering\"\n   759\t         :dao.stream.remote-channel/no-transport\n   760\t         \"this host has no WebSocket dialer\"\n   761\t         (str failure))\n   762\t       \"; dialing it again\"))\n   763\t\n   764\t\n   765\t(defn- step-link\n   766\t  \"Advance the dial of `principal`'s board at `now`: compose one when\n   767\t   due, step it, hand a fresh reflection to the follower, and redial a\n   768\t   dial that is lost.  Liveness is the channel's: a resolve or a read\n   769\t   left unanswered for the link's `give-up-after` is lost as\n   770\t   channel-gone.  Only the address the principal was given is dialed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
