{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc | sed -n '1,460p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yin.repl.index\n     2\t  \"The shell's code indexer: a `dao.space.index` observer on `program-out`\n     3\t   (docs/design/yin.repl.dao.space-index.md).\n     4\t\n     5\t   It is a peer of the evaluator's observer on the same medium, attached\n     6\t   independently and advanced by the evaluation round, never by the\n     7\t   evaluator: neither knows the other.  Each expanded tree packet `[root\n     8\t   rows]` it observes is projected to local `[e a v t m]` AST facts\n     9\t   (yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md §6.5) and committed as ONE atomic transaction\n    10\t   record through a `dao.space.transactor`, which allocates `t`; this\n    11\t   namespace supplies no clock.  Every row of a committed packet is\n    12\t   materialized into the `dao.jing` store in the same round, so its\n    13\t   `:yin/address` facts name content the store holds (yin.vm.linker.dht.md\n    14\t   5.1, rows every round).  After a round that committed, the covered\n    15\t   indexes are published through `dao.space.index` into that round's\n    16\t   own fresh intake, the intake is drained into the `dao.jing` store, the\n    17\t   manifest is read back, and the intake is dropped. Between rounds the\n    18\t   composition retains the transactor's allocator and a verified covered\n    19\t   frontier: its log cursor, manifest and transaction count. Each fresh\n    20\t   publication folds only the committed suffix into the previous covered\n    21\t   roots and emits their dirty subgraph through `dao.space.index`.\n    22\t\n    23\t   Publication still completes synchronously every evaluation. Initial\n    24\t   publication and recovery reconstruct the full authoritative history;\n    25\t   no saved process cursor or allocator is trusted on restart. Incremental\n    26\t   tree mutation removes repeated prefix construction, but does not promise\n    27\t   a fixed wall-time bound on hashing, storage or other round work.\n    28\t\n    29\t   Every `e` is a transactor-local entity id; the only durable name in the\n    30\t   projection is the `:yin/address` fact each node occurrence carries back\n    31\t   to its row address.  `m` is a local metadata entity, one per program,\n    32\t   carrying `:db/op`, the shell's stable session token, the program's root\n    33\t   address, and the round.  Only code is indexed: no printed output, last\n    34\t   value, or evaluation result enters.\n    35\t\n    36\t   Loss is reported, never hidden, and never stops the evaluator (owner\n    37\t   ruling, 2026-09-28): a gap is counted on the observer (`:ingress-gaps`)\n    38\t   and marks the indexer `:lost?`, after which it consumes packets without\n    39\t   indexing any until reset rebuilds it; a packet that could not be\n    40\t   committed, or a publication that did not become readable, is recorded\n    41\t   under `:failure`, never counted as indexed.  `notice` renders what a\n    42\t   round lost for the shell's round result, and `status` is the\n    43\t   evaluator-independent view `repl-state` reports.  Everything here is a\n    44\t   session-composition value; reset and VM selection rebuild it with the\n    45\t   session.  Over a durable store a new process's indexer is seeded from\n    46\t   the recovered snapshot (`rehydrate`), and a rebuilt session's continues\n    47\t   the old one's index (`carry-over`), so `t` and entity allocation never\n    48\t   restart there.\"\n    49\t  (:require [dao.datom :as datom]\n    50\t            [dao.jing :as jing]\n    51\t            [dao.space.index :as index]\n    52\t            [dao.space.transactor :as transactor]\n    53\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n    54\t            [dao.stream.memory-log :as memory-log]\n    55\t            [dao.stream.observer :as observer]\n    56\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n    57\t            [yin.vm.macro :as macro]))\n    58\t\n    59\t\n    60\t;; =============================================================================\n    61\t;; The §6.5 projection\n    62\t;; =============================================================================\n    63\t\n    64\t(defn- assign-local-ids\n    65\t  \"Give every node occurrence of `node`, the map AST rebuilt from row `id`,\n    66\t   a fresh local entity id as its `:eid`, pairing it with its row through\n    67\t   the §2.3 slot table.  Distinct occurrences of one shared row get distinct\n    68\t   ids, so `vm/ast->datoms` emits every occurrence exactly as it does for a\n    69\t   tree without `:eid`s.  `acc` is `[next-e addresses]`; answers\n    70\t   `[node' acc']`, `addresses` mapping each id to its row address.\"\n    71\t  [rows node id [next-e addresses]]\n    72\t  (let [row (get rows id)\n    73\t        slots (get vm/semantic-bytecode-grammar (:type node))\n    74\t        child (fn [acc child-node child-id]\n    75\t                (assign-local-ids rows child-node child-id acc))]\n    76\t    (reduce\n    77\t      (fn [[node acc] [i [field kind]]]\n    78\t        (let [slot (nth row (+ 2 i))]\n    79\t          (case kind\n    80\t            :node (let [[c acc'] (child acc (get node field) slot)]\n    81\t                    [(assoc node field c) acc'])\n    82\t            :nodes (let [[cs acc']\n    83\t                         (reduce (fn [[cs acc] [c cid]]\n    84\t                                   (let [[c' acc'] (child acc c cid)]\n    85\t                                     [(conj cs c') acc']))\n    86\t                                 [[] acc]\n    87\t                                 (map vector (get node field) slot))]\n    88\t                     [(assoc node field cs) acc'])\n    89\t            [node acc])))\n    90\t      [(assoc node :eid next-e) [(inc next-e) (assoc addresses next-e id)]]\n    91\t      (map-indexed vector slots))))\n    92\t\n    93\t\n    94\t(defn packet->tx-data\n    95\t  \"Project one expanded tree packet to transactor tx-data, allocating local\n    96\t   entity ids from `next-e`.  `provenance` is `{:session-token s :round r}`.\n    97\t\n    98\t   Answers `{:tx-data [...] :next-e n :meta-e m :root root}`: the metadata\n    99\t   entity's facts, then `vm/ast->datoms` of the expanded tree under `m`,\n   100\t   then one `[e :yin/address addr]` per node occurrence.  Every datom leaves\n   101\t   `t` nil, which the transactor stamps.\"\n   102\t  [packet next-e {:keys [session-token round]}]\n   103\t  (let [{:keys [root rows], :as row-set} (macro/packet->row-set packet)\n   104\t        meta-e next-e\n   105\t        [ast [next-e' addresses]] (assign-local-ids\n   106\t                                    rows\n   107\t                                    (vm/semantic-bytecode->ast row-set)\n   108\t                                    root\n   109\t                                    [(inc meta-e) {}])\n   110\t        facts (vm/ast->datoms ast {:m meta-e})\n   111\t        untimed (fn [e a v m] [e a v nil m])]\n   112\t    (when-let [stray (some (fn [[e]] (when (neg? e) e)) facts)]\n   113\t      (throw (ex-info \"projected node escaped local id assignment\"\n   114\t                      {:e stray, :root root})))\n   115\t    {:tx-data (-> [(untimed meta-e :db/op :db/assert datom/default-op)\n   116\t                   (untimed meta-e :yin.repl/session session-token\n   117\t                            datom/default-op)\n   118\t                   (untimed meta-e :yin.repl/root root datom/default-op)\n   119\t                   (untimed meta-e :yin.repl/round round datom/default-op)]\n   120\t                  (into (map (fn [[e a v _t m]] (untimed e a v m))) facts)\n   121\t                  (into (map (fn [[e addr]]\n   122\t                               (untimed e :yin/address addr meta-e)))\n   123\t                        (sort-by key addresses))),\n   124\t     :next-e next-e',\n   125\t     :meta-e meta-e,\n   126\t     :root root\n   127\t     :row-set row-set}))\n   128\t\n   129\t\n   130\t;; =============================================================================\n   131\t;; The indexer value\n   132\t;; =============================================================================\n   133\t\n   134\t(defn- memory-log\n   135\t  []\n   136\t  (:dao.stream/handle\n   137\t    (memory-log/create! {:dao.stream/type memory-log/transport-type})))\n   138\t\n   139\t\n   140\t(defn make-indexer\n   141\t  \"The indexer for one session: `observer`, attached to `program-out`\n   142\t   beside the evaluator's; `:local`, the complete-retention log its\n   143\t   transactions are committed to (dao.space.transactor requires memory-log\n   144\t   retention); and `content-store`, the `dao.jing` byte store publications\n   145\t   materialize into.  `session-token` is the shell's stable token, recorded\n   146\t   as provenance; `publish-opts` reach `transactor/publish!` as-is.\n   147\t\n   148\t   `after-publish` is `(fn [manifest-address])`, called after a round's\n   149\t   manifest is read back from the store and before the round is reported\n   150\t   published: the durable store's HEAD write, which is what makes the\n   151\t   round durably published (docs/design/yin.repl.dao.space-index.md).\n   152\t   Nil — the memory store — publishes exactly as before.\n   153\t\n   154\t   `:allocator` retains only the transactor authority, with its intake\n   155\t   detached. `:materialization` retains verified coverage as plain data:\n   156\t   `{:cursor c :transactions n :manifest-address a :manifest m :max-t t}`.\n   157\t   A round's fresh `:publication` intake, pool and tree builder are dropped\n   158\t   at its end; no earlier publication payload is retained.\"\n   159\t  [{:keys [observer session-token content-store publish-opts after-publish]}]\n   160\t  {:observer observer\n   161\t   :local (memory-log)\n   162\t   :content-store content-store\n   163\t   :session-token session-token\n   164\t   :publish-opts publish-opts\n   165\t   :after-publish after-publish\n   166\t   :next-e datom/first-user-id\n   167\t   :transactions 0\n   168\t   :published 0\n   169\t   :published-payloads 0\n   170\t   :manifest-address nil\n   171\t   :allocator nil\n   172\t   :materialization nil\n   173\t   :lost? false\n   174\t   :failure nil})\n   175\t\n   176\t\n   177\t(defn- next-entity-id\n   178\t  \"One greater than the greatest entity or metadata-entity id `datoms`\n   179\t   use, never below `datom/first-user-id`.\"\n   180\t  [datoms]\n   181\t  (reduce (fn [next-e [e _a _v _t m]]\n   182\t            (cond-> next-e\n   183\t              (integer? e) (max (inc e))\n   184\t              (integer? m) (max (inc m))))\n   185\t          datom/first-user-id\n   186\t          datoms))\n   187\t\n   188\t\n   189\t(defn rehydrate\n   190\t  \"Seed a fresh indexer from a recovered durable snapshot, `{:manifest\n   191\t   address :datoms [...]}` (yin.repl.store's `:recovery`), before any\n   192\t   evaluation is admitted.  Its log becomes a fresh complete-retention\n   193\t   memory log holding the recovered datoms as transaction records, one\n   194\t   per original `t` in ascending order, each datom and its `t` preserved,\n   195\t   so a new transactor derives the next `t` from it. Entity\n   196\t   allocation resumes one past the greatest restored entity or metadata\n   197\t   id.  The manifest is the published one, covering every restored\n   198\t   transaction, so `q` answers from it before anything new is evaluated.\n   199\t   Restored facts keep their original session tokens and round metadata:\n   200\t   they are the datoms as committed.  A recovery without a manifest is an\n   201\t   empty index. Live allocation and publication successors are always\n   202\t   discarded, including any stale or foreign cursor: the first subsequent\n   203\t   publication takes the full reconstruction path and derives a new cursor\n   204\t   from this log, never from a saved process checkpoint.\"\n   205\t  [indexer {:keys [manifest datoms]}]\n   206\t  (if (nil? manifest)\n   207\t    (assoc indexer :allocator nil :materialization nil)\n   208\t    (let [log (memory-log)\n   209\t          by-t (group-by index/datom-t datoms)\n   210\t          ts (sort (keys by-t))]\n   211\t      (doseq [t ts]\n   212\t        (let [answer (stream/append! log {:dao.space/transaction\n   213\t                                          {:t t, :datoms (vec (get by-t t))}})]\n   214\t          (when-not (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome answer))\n   215\t            (throw (ex-info \"the recovered snapshot could not be rehydrated\"\n   216\t                            {:t t, :outcome answer})))))\n   217\t      (assoc indexer\n   218\t             :local log\n   219\t             :next-e (next-entity-id datoms)\n   220\t             :transactions (count ts)\n   221\t             :published (count ts)\n   222\t             :allocator nil\n   223\t             :materialization nil\n   224\t             :manifest-address manifest))))\n   225\t\n   226\t\n   227\t(defn carry-over\n   228\t  \"A rebuilt session's fresh `indexer`, continuing `previous`'s index: its\n   229\t   transaction log, entity allocation, counts, published manifest, and\n   230\t   live allocator/verified materialization successors.\n   231\t   `(reset)` and VM selection over a durable store use it, so a rebuild\n   232\t   never resets `t` or entity allocation and `q` keeps answering the\n   233\t   published index; the observer is the new session's, and a lost or\n   234\t   failed indexer is recovered by the rebuild as it is today.\"\n   235\t  [indexer previous]\n   236\t  (merge indexer\n   237\t         (select-keys previous [:local :next-e :transactions :published\n   238\t                                :published-payloads :manifest-address\n   239\t                                :allocator :materialization :unwritten])))\n   240\t\n   241\t\n   242\t(defn- open-publication\n   243\t  \"The round's transactor and the `dao.jing` pool observer over its intake.\n   244\t   The retained allocator remains the transactor's authority; when absent\n   245\t   or bound to another log, create! derives it from authoritative history.\n   246\t   No caller-supplied clock is accepted. The intake is\n   247\t   complete-retention: `publish-index!` appends every node blob before the\n   248\t   manifest and the round drains only after it returns, so an evicting\n   249\t   intake would lose the head of any publication larger than its capacity\n   250\t   and that publication could never complete.\"\n   251\t  [ix]\n   252\t  (if (:publication ix)\n   253\t    ix\n   254\t    (let [intake (memory-log)\n   255\t          allocator (:allocator ix)\n   256\t          tx (if (and allocator\n   257\t                      (identical? (:local ix) (:local-stream allocator)))\n   258\t               (transactor/with-intake-pool allocator [intake])\n   259\t               (transactor/create! {:local-stream (:local ix)\n   260\t                                    :intake-pool [intake]\n   261\t                                    :name \"yin.repl.index\"}))]\n   262\t      (assoc ix\n   263\t             :allocator (transactor/with-intake-pool tx nil)\n   264\t             :publication\n   265\t             {:transactor tx\n   266\t              :intake intake\n   267\t              :pool (jing/observer-state\n   268\t                      [{:stream intake\n   269\t                        :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor\n   270\t                                  (stream/cursor intake\n   271\t                                                 :dao.stream/oldest))}])}))))\n   272\t\n   273\t\n   274\t(defn- write-rows\n   275\t  \"Put the rows of every committed program not yet written into the index\n   276\t   store, oldest first (yin.vm.linker.dht.md 5.1, owner decision 1: rows\n   277\t   every round), so `:yin/address` facts name content the store holds.\n   278\t   `:unwritten` holds those programs' row sets.  A put that fails stops\n   279\t   the writing: it and every later row set stay `:unwritten`, and the\n   280\t   round's failure is stage `:materialize`.  Once nothing is unwritten, a\n   281\t   `:materialize` failure is recovered and cleared.  No publication is\n   282\t   made while anything is unwritten, so a HEAD never moves over a missing\n   283\t   row.\"\n   284\t  [ix round]\n   285\t  (loop [ix ix]\n   286\t    (if-let [row-set (first (:unwritten ix))]\n   287\t      (let [failed (try (vm/materialize-tree! (:content-store ix) row-set)\n   288\t                        nil\n   289\t                        (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) e\n   290\t                          {:round round\n   291\t                           :stage :materialize\n   292\t                           :root (:root row-set)\n   293\t                           :message (ex-message e)}))]\n   294\t        (if failed\n   295\t          (assoc ix :failure failed)\n   296\t          (recur (update ix :unwritten (comp vec rest)))))\n   297\t      (cond-> (dissoc ix :unwritten)\n   298\t        (= :materialize (:stage (:failure ix))) (dissoc :failure)))))\n   299\t\n   300\t\n   301\t(defn- commit\n   302\t  \"Commit one packet as one transaction; its rows join `:unwritten`, which\n   303\t   the round writes before it publishes (`write-rows`).  A packet that\n   304\t   could not be projected or committed is consumed and recorded as the\n   305\t   failure, never counted, and materializes nothing.\"\n   306\t  [ix packet round]\n   307\t  (try\n   308\t    (let [{:keys [tx-data next-e root row-set]}\n   309\t          (packet->tx-data packet\n   310\t                           (:next-e ix)\n   311\t                           {:session-token (:session-token ix), :round round})\n   312\t          answer (transactor/transact! (get-in ix [:publication :transactor])\n   313\t                                       tx-data)]\n   314\t      (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome answer))\n   315\t        [(-> ix\n   316\t             (assoc :next-e next-e)\n   317\t             (update :transactions inc)\n   318\t             (update :unwritten (fnil conj []) row-set))\n   319\t         true]\n   320\t        [(assoc ix\n   321\t                :failure {:round round\n   322\t                          :root root\n   323\t                          :stage :transact\n   324\t                          :outcome (:dao.stream/outcome answer)})\n   325\t         false]))\n   326\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) e\n   327\t      [(assoc ix\n   328\t              :failure {:round round\n   329\t                        :stage :project\n   330\t                        :message (ex-message e)})\n   331\t       false])))\n   332\t\n   333\t\n   334\t(defn- materialize\n   335\t  \"Drain the intake into the store until it blocks.  Answers how many\n   336\t   payloads it materialized and, when the drain met a gap or a defect, what\n   337\t   it met.  The pool is not kept: its intake is dropped with the round.\"\n   338\t  [content-store pool]\n   339\t  (loop [pool pool\n   340\t         n 0]\n   341\t    (let [{:keys [signal], :as r} (jing/observe-step! content-store pool)]\n   342\t      (case signal\n   343\t        :dao.stream/ok\n   344\t        (let [missing #?(:cljd (Object.) :clj (Object.) :cljs (js-obj))]\n   345\t          ;; Every emitted dirty node reads back before HEAD moves. The\n   346\t          ;; unchanged subgraphs were verified by earlier publications;\n   347\t          ;; immutable retained content makes that verification reusable.\n   348\t          (when (identical? missing (jing/get content-store (:address r) missing))\n   349\t            (throw (ex-info \"published content could not be read back\"\n   350\t                            {:address (:address r)})))\n   351\t          (recur (:state r) (inc n)))\n   352\t        :dao.stream/blocked [n nil]\n   353\t        [n signal]))))\n   354\t\n   355\t\n   356\t(defn- suffix-state\n   357\t  \"Restore verified roots and fold only records after their cursor. The\n   358\t   expected record count independently validates the cursor against this\n   359\t   composition's one-record-per-transaction log. A stale/foreign cursor,\n   360\t   mismatched frontier or rejected record returns nil: the caller must\n   361\t   reconstruct in full, never publish an uncertain suffix.\"\n   362\t  [ix intake]\n   363\t  (let [{:keys [cursor transactions manifest-address manifest max-t]}\n   364\t        (:materialization ix)]\n   365\t    (when (and manifest-address\n   366\t               (= manifest-address (:manifest-address ix))\n   367\t               (= transactions (:published ix))\n   368\t               (= (:branching-factor manifest)\n   369\t                  (:branching-factor (:publish-opts ix) 512)))\n   370\t      (try\n   371\t        (let [candidate {:manifest-address manifest-address\n   372\t                         :mode :resolved :schema-address (jing/segment-key {})\n   373\t                         :ids nil :batch transactions :max-t max-t :rejected 0}\n   374\t              consumer (index/restore candidate\n   375\t                                      {:content-store (:content-store ix)\n   376\t                                       :intake intake :mode :resolved :schema {}})\n   377\t              expected (- (:transactions ix) transactions)]\n   378\t          (loop [cursor cursor, consumer consumer, n 0]\n   379\t            (let [r (stream/next (:local ix) cursor)]\n   380\t              (when (stream/valid-outcome? :next r)\n   381\t                (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\n   382\t                  :dao.stream/ok\n   383\t                  (when (< n expected)\n   384\t                    (let [consumer' (index/fold-batch consumer (:dao.stream/value r))]\n   385\t                      (when (zero? (:rejected consumer'))\n   386\t                        (recur (:dao.stream/cursor r) consumer' (inc n)))))\n   387\t                  (:dao.stream/blocked :dao.stream/end)\n   388\t                  (when (= n expected) {:cursor cursor :consumer consumer})\n   389\t                  nil)))))\n   390\t        (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) _\n   391\t          nil)))))\n   392\t\n   393\t\n   394\t(defn- enqueue-publication\n   395\t  \"Full reconstruction when no validated frontier is available; otherwise\n   396\t   publication of the suffix-folded trees through the existing indexer.\"\n   397\t  [ix]\n   398\t  (let [{:keys [transactor intake]} (:publication ix)]\n   399\t    (if-let [{:keys [cursor consumer]} (suffix-state ix intake)]\n   400\t      (let [;; A fresh round has exactly one intake; still honor the\n   401\t            ;; caller's selection function and its pool-membership rule.\n   402\t            select-stream (:select-stream (:publish-opts ix) first)\n   403\t            selected (when (fn? select-stream) (select-stream [intake]))\n   404\t            _ (when-not (identical? selected intake)\n   405\t                (throw (ex-info \"publication must select its round's intake\" {})))\n   406\t            {:keys [status state]} (index/publish! consumer)\n   407\t            manifest (get-in state [:publish :manifest])]\n   408\t        (when-not (= :ok status)\n   409\t          (throw (ex-info \"complete-retention publication intake refused\" {:status status})))\n   410\t        {:cursor cursor :manifest manifest :manifest-address (jing/segment-key manifest)})\n   411\t      (let [result (transactor/publish! transactor (:publish-opts ix))\n   412\t            tail (stream/cursor (:local ix) :dao.stream/newest)]\n   413\t        (when-not (and (stream/valid-outcome? :cursor tail)\n   414\t                       (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome tail)))\n   415\t          (throw (ex-info \"published log frontier could not be read\" {:result tail})))\n   416\t        (assoc result :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor tail))))))\n   417\t\n   418\t\n   419\t(defn- publish\n   420\t  \"Publish the covered indexes over every committed transaction, using\n   421\t   the retained frontier when valid, drain the intake, and read the\n   422\t   manifest back from it.  Only a publication whose manifest the store\n   423\t   answers becomes the reported one, covering `:published` transactions;\n   424\t   in durable mode the HEAD pointer moves — `after-publish` — only after\n   425\t   that read-back, so a HEAD never names a manifest the store cannot\n   426\t   answer, and a HEAD that cannot be written leaves the round reported\n   427\t   unpublished.\"\n   428\t  [ix round]\n   429\t  (try\n   430\t    (let [{:keys [pool]} (:publication ix)\n   431\t          {:keys [manifest-address manifest cursor]} (enqueue-publication ix)\n   432\t          [n defect] (materialize (:content-store ix) pool)]\n   433\t      (if defect\n   434\t        (assoc ix :failure {:round round :stage :materialize :outcome defect})\n   435\t        (do (index/read-manifest (:content-store ix) manifest-address)\n   436\t            (when-some [write-head! (:after-publish ix)]\n   437\t              (write-head! manifest-address))\n   438\t            (cond-> (assoc ix\n   439\t                           :manifest-address manifest-address\n   440\t                           :published (:transactions ix)\n   441\t                           :published-payloads n\n   442\t                           :materialization {:cursor cursor\n   443\t                                             :transactions (:transactions ix)\n   444\t                                             :manifest-address manifest-address\n   445\t                                             :manifest manifest\n   446\t                                             :max-t (dec (transactor/watermark (:allocator ix)))})\n   447\t              (= :publish (:stage (:failure ix))) (assoc :failure nil)))))\n   448\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) e\n   449\t      (assoc ix\n   450\t             :failure {:round round :stage :publish :message (ex-message e)}))))\n   451\t\n   452\t\n   453\t(defn- consume\n   454\t  \"Advance the observer past every packet still on the medium, handing each\n   455\t   to `f` with the indexer; a gap marks the indexer lost, after which no\n   456\t   packet reaches `f`.\"\n   457\t  [indexer f]\n   458\t  (loop [ix indexer]\n   459\t    (let [{:keys [status batch] observer' :observer}\n   460\t          (observer/observe-next (:observer ix))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc | sed -n '860,990p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc | sed -n '870,1090p'; rg -n 'dht|step-owner|publish-opts' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc | sed -n '860,990p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc | sed -n '870,1090p'; rg -n 'dht|step-owner|publish-opts' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"   860\t   its HEAD read and the snapshot it names validated — a corrupt HEAD\n   861\t   or snapshot refuses construction, and a second owner of the directory\n   862\t   is refused naming it.  The spec is resolved and the store opened once\n   863\t   here, never switched at runtime, and supplying it together with\n   864\t   `index-store` (a handle injected directly) is refused.\n   865\t\n   866\t   `:index-recovery` carries what the durable open recovered —\n   867\t   `{:manifest <address or nil> :datoms <the validated snapshot or nil>}`\n   868\t   — and the indexer is rehydrated from it here, before any evaluation\n   869\t   is admitted (`yin.repl.index/rehydrate`): `q` answers the previous\n   870\t   run's facts, which keep their own session tokens, while this process\n   871\t   mints a new token for its own.  In durable mode `(reset)` and `(vm …)`\n   872\t   carry the index across the rebuild; with the memory store they start\n   873\t   an empty one, as they always have.\n   874\t\n   875\t   `{:type :dht :dir dir ...}` is the DHT store (yin.repl.dht): that\n   876\t   durable directory store with a `dao.jing.dht` node composed over it.\n   877\t   Its step-owner value is `:dht`, advanced only by `yin.repl.dht/step`\n   878\t   from the host's ticker; a round publishes against the local store and\n   879\t   never waits on it.  It is also the link source\n   880\t   (yin.vm.linker.dht.md 4.1): a `(require ...)` of a name `name-env`\n   881\t   resolves starts a closure load on the node, which may fetch from\n   882\t   peers, and parks until the load ends; `content-store` and\n   883\t   `content-client` are refused with it.\n   884\t\n   885\t   `:dht-key` is the publisher's stable key `{:seed :public}`, loaded\n   886\t   from its key file by the host (yin.vm.linker.dht.md 6.5); without it\n   887\t   `(yin.link/publish ...)` is refused and the node still reads, resolves,\n   888\t   loads and links.  `:principals` are the public keys whose signed name\n   889\t   assertions the reader honors (7.1); a key's own principal is declared\n   890\t   with them.\n   891\t\n   892\t   A DHT store spec's `:follow` entries are the principals whose\n   893\t   published heads the node follows (yin.vm.linker.dht.head.md 5.5);\n   894\t   `:ws-host` is the host WebSocket seam (yin.repl.host) the head board\n   895\t   is served and dialed over, and `:write-heads!` the file replace\n   896\t   `heads.edn` is written with (yin.repl.dht/open).  A `(require ...)` of\n   897\t   a name that is absent while a followed principal has no installed\n   898\t   head stays pending until that head is installed.\n   899\t\n   900\t   `:custody` is an optional custody composition value\n   901\t   (yin.vm.ucf.compose): the shell only carries it, as data, so the\n   902\t   host's single step owner can advance it (yin.repl.main/step-all --\n   903\t   the custody control step runs during hydration and through the\n   904\t   bounded shutdown drain; the custody program step runs only while\n   905\t   the shell is admitted and running).  Nothing in the shell reads or\n   906\t   steps it; nil, the default, is today's behaviour.\n   907\t\n   908\t   `:frontends` is the frontend catalog (`yang.frontend`) the session\n   909\t   compiles through, composed by the host entry point (this namespace\n   910\t   requires no frontend; see `yin.repl.frontends`).  Without it the catalog\n   911\t   is empty and every compile answers `unavailable-parser`.  The session\n   912\t   pins this immutable snapshot: installing into another catalog value\n   913\t   never changes a live session.  `:lang` selects a frontend by id\n   914\t   (`:yang/python`) or by `[id revision]`; a language keyword is not a\n   915\t   selector. The default is the `:yang/clojure` frontend.\n   916\t   one the catalog cannot answer is an `unavailable-parser` diagnostic,\n   917\t   never a fallback to another frontend.\"\n   918\t  ([] (create-state {}))\n   919\t  ([{:keys [lang output-cursor output-stream vm-type primitives\n   920\t            content-store content-client name-env link-policy index-store\n   921\t            index-store-spec dht-key principals ws-host write-heads! custody\n   922\t            frontends admission]\n   923\t     :or {lang :yang/clojure vm-type :semantic admission {}}}]\n   924\t   (let [output-stream (or output-stream (make-output-medium!))\n   925\t         output-cursor (or output-cursor (mint-cursor output-stream))\n   926\t         shell-token (str (random-uuid))\n   927\t         index-store-spec (cond\n   928\t                            (and index-store index-store-spec)\n   929\t                            (throw (ex-info\n   930\t                                     (str \"yin.repl/create-state takes one \"\n   931\t                                          \"index store: :index-store-spec \"\n   932\t                                          \"(mem or a file directory) or \"\n   933\t                                          \":index-store (a dao.jing handle), \"\n   934\t                                          \"not both\")\n   935\t                                     {:index-store-spec index-store-spec}))\n   936\t\n   937\t                            index-store nil\n   938\t\n   939\t                            :else (store/checked-spec index-store-spec))\n   940\t         ;; composed before the store opens: a refused composition never\n   941\t         ;; holds a directory lock\n   942\t         link-source (link/composition\n   943\t                       {:name-env name-env\n   944\t                        :content-store content-store\n   945\t                        :content-client content-client\n   946\t                        :dht? (= :dht (:type index-store-spec))\n   947\t                        :principals principals\n   948\t                        :key dht-key\n   949\t                        :admission (when-not (= :external admission)\n   950\t                                     admission)\n   951\t                        :follow (when (= :dht (:type index-store-spec))\n   952\t                                  (repl.dht/followed-principals\n   953\t                                    index-store-spec))})\n   954\t         index-store (or index-store\n   955\t                         (if (= :dht (:type index-store-spec))\n   956\t                           (repl.dht/open index-store-spec\n   957\t                                          {:key dht-key\n   958\t                                           :ws ws-host\n   959\t                                           :write-heads! write-heads!})\n   960\t                           (store/open index-store-spec)))]\n   961\t     (merge\n   962\t       (update (make-session vm-type output-stream\n   963\t                             (merge (selected-primitives frontends lang)\n   964\t                                    primitives)\n   965\t                             shell-token\n   966\t                             index-store link-source)\n   967\t               :indexer index/rehydrate (:recovery index-store))\n   968\t       {:lang lang\n   969\t        :frontends (or frontends frontend/empty-catalog)\n   970\t        :vm-type vm-type\n   971\t        :extra-primitives primitives\n   972\t        :output-stream output-stream\n   973\t        :output-cursor output-cursor\n   974\t        :ledger {:output :untried}\n   975\t        :shell-token shell-token\n   976\t        :index-store (repl.dht/without-runner index-store)\n   977\t        :index-store-spec index-store-spec\n   978\t        :dht (:dht index-store)\n   979\t        :index-recovery (or (:recovery index-store)\n   980\t                            {:manifest nil :datoms nil})\n   981\t        :round 0\n   982\t        :ingress-loss? false\n   983\t        :last-value nil\n   984\t        :last-value-2 nil\n   985\t        :last-value-3 nil\n   986\t        :pending-input nil\n   987\t        :link-source link-source\n   988\t        :admission admission\n   989\t        :initial-admission admission\n   990\t        :link-policy (checked-link-policy link-policy)\n   870\t                                                   (ex-data e))\n   871\t                                          e))))\n   872\t                    made (assoc :startup-lines made)\n   873\t                    adapter (assoc :adapter adapter))]\n   874\t         (if-some [path (:dht-keygen opts)]\n   875\t           (keygen! path)\n   876\t           (let [key (some-> (:dht-key-file opts) load-key)\n   877\t                 opts (cond-> opts\n   878\t                        key (assoc :publisher (sign/principal (:public key))))\n   879\t                 ;; the head board is served and dialed over the host's\n   880\t                 ;; WebSocket seam (yin.vm.linker.dht.head.md 5.1)\n   881\t                 state' (boot (assoc opts\n   882\t                                     :dht-key key\n   883\t                                     :ws-host (or (:adapter opts)\n   884\t                                                  (host/websocket))))\n   885\t                 server (boot-server opts)\n   886\t                 lines (into (vec (repl.dht/follow-lines (:repl state')))\n   887\t                             (when node-dir\n   888\t                               (save-state! node-dir saved resolved reset?)))]\n   889\t             {:opts (cond-> opts\n   890\t                      (seq lines) (update :startup-lines\n   891\t                                          #(into (vec %) lines)))\n   892\t              :state state'\n   893\t              :server server}))))\n   894\t     (catch #?(:cljd Object\n   895\t               :clj Throwable\n   896\t               :cljs :default)\n   897\t            e\n   898\t       (if (ex-data e)\n   899\t         {:refusal (or (ex-message e) (str e))}\n   900\t         (throw e))))))\n   901\t\n   902\t\n   903\t(defn- refuse!\n   904\t  \"Print why the composition refused to start and end the process with a\n   905\t   failing status, so a refused startup never looks like a working shell.\"\n   906\t  [refusal]\n   907\t  (println refusal)\n   908\t  #?(:cljd (io/exit 1)\n   909\t     :jolt (do (flush) (System/exit 1))\n   910\t     :clj (.halt (Runtime/getRuntime) 1)\n   911\t     :cljs (.exit js/process 1)))\n   912\t\n   913\t\n   914\t(defn- custody-of\n   915\t  [state]\n   916\t  (get-in state [:repl :custody]))\n   917\t\n   918\t\n   919\t(defn close-index-store!\n   920\t  \"Release the composition's lifecycle resources before the host exits:\n   921\t   the custody composition's journals first (compose/close! -- the\n   922\t   authority and every journal backend the composition opened; it never\n   923\t   throws, so a failed close never blocks the exit), then the index\n   924\t   store's own resources (in durable mode, the exclusive directory\n   925\t   lock).  The shell has already stopped when a host calls this; the\n   926\t   memory store has nothing to release.  A DHT store's head board and\n   927\t   dials have been asked to stop and drained by then (`stop-tick`);\n   928\t   `yin.repl.dht/close!` is the last resort for whatever the budget\n   929\t   left.\"\n   930\t  [state]\n   931\t  (when-some [c (custody-of state)]\n   932\t    (compose/close! c))\n   933\t  (repl.dht/close! (:repl state))\n   934\t  (store/close! (get-in state [:repl :index-store])))\n   935\t\n   936\t\n   937\t(defn- entry-text\n   938\t  [entry]\n   939\t  (or (get entry driver/text-key) (get entry serve/text-key)))\n   940\t\n   941\t\n   942\t(defn banner\n   943\t  \"Text the composition prints before the first prompt, given parsed\n   944\t   options.  A DHT store states here (before its node steps once, so\n   945\t   before anything is shared) what it will share: the whole store when\n   946\t   `--dht-publish` is given, nothing otherwise (yin.repl.dht/banner).\"\n   947\t  [opts]\n   948\t  (let [spec (:index-store-spec opts)\n   949\t        dht? (= :dht (:type spec))]\n   950\t    (cond-> (vec (:startup-lines opts))\n   951\t      (seq (:rejected opts)) (conj telemetry-text)\n   952\t      (and (:port opts) (zero? (:port opts)))\n   953\t      (conj (str \"serving on all interfaces on an ephemeral port; the Serving\"\n   954\t                 \" line names it once bound. Anyone who can reach this port\"\n   955\t                 \" can evaluate code in this shell; there is no\"\n   956\t                 \" authentication.\"))\n   957\t\n   958\t      (and (:port opts) (not (zero? (:port opts))))\n   959\t      (conj (str \"serving on all interfaces: ws://127.0.0.1:\" (:port opts)\n   960\t                 (let [ip (local-ip)]\n   961\t                   (if (= \"127.0.0.1\" ip)\n   962\t                     \" and ws://<this machine's IP>:\"\n   963\t                     (str \" and ws://\" ip \":\")))\n   964\t                 (:port opts)\n   965\t                 \". Anyone who can reach this port can evaluate code in this\"\n   966\t                 \" shell; there is no authentication.\"))\n   967\t      (and (:headless? opts) (not (:port opts)))\n   968\t      (conj \"--headless has nothing to attend without a served endpoint\")\n   969\t      dht? (into (repl.dht/banner spec))\n   970\t      (and dht? (:publish? spec))\n   971\t      (conj (str \"dht: the code index and the code itself are shared: every\"\n   972\t                 \" evaluated program's rows are written to the index store\"\n   973\t                 \" each round\"))\n   974\t      (and dht? (:publisher opts))\n   975\t      (conj (str \"dht: names published here are signed by principal \"\n   976\t                 (:publisher opts) \" (key from \" (:dht-key-file opts) \")\"))\n   977\t      (and dht? (not (:publisher opts)))\n   978\t      (conj (str \"dht: no --dht-key: (yin.link/publish ...) is refused; names\"\n   979\t                 \" are still read, resolved, loaded and linked\"))\n   980\t      #?(:cljd false :jolt true :default false)\n   981\t      (into [shell/host-text\n   982\t             ;; J5: the native parser is disclosed; with no usable library\n   983\t             ;; Python is left out of the catalog and the reason is printed\n   984\t             #?(:jolt (if (python.antlr.parser/available?)\n   985\t                        (str \"python: the native C++ ANTLR4 parser\"\n   986\t                             \" (native/jolt-parser), in process; no process\"\n   987\t                             \" crash isolation\")\n   988\t                        \"python: unavailable-parser (the native parser library is missing or incompatible; bb build:jolt-native)\")\n   989\t                :default nil)]))))\n   990\t\n   991\t\n   992\t(defn- exit-with!\n   993\t  \"Print a composition that ends at startup -- `--dht-keygen` -- and end\n   994\t   the process with its status.\"\n   995\t  [{:keys [lines exit]}]\n   996\t  (doseq [line lines]\n   997\t    (println line))\n   998\t  #?(:cljd (io/exit exit)\n   999\t     :jolt (do (flush) (System/exit exit))\n  1000\t     :clj (.halt (Runtime/getRuntime) (int exit))\n  1001\t     :cljs (.exit js/process exit)))\n  1002\t\n  1003\t\n  1004\t(defn- custody-control-step\n  1005\t  \"The custody control plane's tick (r3 1.12): the renewals, pending\n  1006\t   releases and request retries of every holder, the judge step and the\n  1007\t   front steps of whatever custody composition the shell carries.  It\n  1008\t   runs immediately after the DHT step and before the refusal and\n  1009\t   admission branches, so custody progress and cleanup do not wait for\n  1010\t   a hydration to finish and survive a refused store.  No program work\n  1011\t   happens here whatever the shell's state.\"\n  1012\t  [state]\n  1013\t  (if-some [c (custody-of state)]\n  1014\t    (assoc-in state [:repl :custody] (compose/control-step c))\n  1015\t    state))\n  1016\t\n  1017\t\n  1018\t(defn- custody-program-step\n  1019\t  \"The custody program step's tick: activation, execution and export\n  1020\t   preparation under the split driver's own revalidated tenure.  It runs\n  1021\t   after the shell's own step and before the endpoint's, and never once\n  1022\t   the shell has stopped -- the stop latch is set in the shell's place.\"\n  1023\t  [state]\n  1024\t  (if-some [c (custody-of state)]\n  1025\t    (assoc-in state [:repl :custody] (compose/program-step c))\n  1026\t    state))\n  1027\t\n  1028\t\n  1029\t(defn- custody-stop\n  1030\t  \"Latch the local stop on every holder of the shell's custody\n  1031\t   composition (compose/stop): program work ends, control cleanup\n  1032\t   continues through the bounded shutdown drain.  Idempotent, and a\n  1033\t   no-op with no composition.\"\n  1034\t  [state]\n  1035\t  (if-some [c (custody-of state)]\n  1036\t    (assoc-in state [:repl :custody] (compose/stop c))\n  1037\t    state))\n  1038\t\n  1039\t\n  1040\t(defn- custody-owed?\n  1041\t  \"True while the shell's custody composition owes a control-plane\n  1042\t   write (compose/owed-control-write?): a pending write keeps the tick\n  1043\t   owner's cadence at the base interval, like the driver's own.\"\n  1044\t  [state]\n  1045\t  (if-some [c (custody-of state)]\n  1046\t    (compose/owed-control-write? c)\n  1047\t    false))\n  1048\t\n  1049\t\n  1050\t(defn step-all\n  1051\t  \"One tick of the single step owner: the local shell first, then the served\n  1052\t   endpoint, against the same shell value.  A DHT index store's node is stepped\n  1053\t   first (yin.repl.dht/step): its lines print before the shell's, a\n  1054\t   hydration still outstanding leaves every typed line waiting in the\n  1055\t   input medium, and a refused one stops the shell.  The custody control\n  1056\t   plane is stepped next, before the refusal and admission branches, so\n  1057\t   renewals, pending releases and request retries continue during\n  1058\t   hydration and past a refusal.  A `--port` process\n  1059\t   serves one shared shell, as v1's atom made it: the driver evaluates this\n  1060\t   tick's local\n  1061\t   lines first, so a definition typed at the local prompt is already in the\n  1062\t   shell the endpoint evaluates remote requests against in the same tick, and\n  1063\t   the endpoint's shell (remote definitions included) is threaded back\n  1064\t   before the next tick.  The custody program step follows the driver's own\n  1065\t   step and precedes the endpoint's; once the shell has stopped it is\n  1066\t   replaced by the stop latch, so no custody program call runs after\n  1067\t   `:running?` turns false.  A require parked on a closure load the node\n  1068\t   ended this tick is re-checked once, before any typed line, with no line\n  1069\t   of its own (yin.repl/recheck-on-tick, yin.vm.linker.dht.md 8.2),\n  1070\t   and linker progress resumes a parked run (7.5): its text prints after the\n  1071\t   node's lines.  Returns `[state server lines]`;\n  1072\t   the caller only prints.\"\n  1073\t  [state server now]\n  1074\t  (let [[repl dht-lines events] (repl.dht/step (:repl state) now)\n  1075\t        state (custody-control-step (assoc state :repl repl))]\n  1076\t    (cond\n  1077\t      (repl.dht/refusal repl)\n  1078\t      [(custody-stop (assoc state :running? false)) server dht-lines]\n  1079\t\n  1080\t      (not (repl.dht/admitting? repl))\n  1081\t      [state server dht-lines]\n  1082\t\n  1083\t      :else\n  1084\t      (let [[repl rechecked] (shell/recheck-on-tick (:repl state) events)\n  1085\t            dht-lines (cond-> dht-lines\n  1086\t                        (seq rechecked) (conj rechecked))\n